namespace __root__
-- The self-hosted toolchain's driver (stage 21, gaps D2-D7 of
-- `wiz-notes/selfhost-parity.md`). It replaces the generated `def main` strings of
-- `Wiz/Selfhost.lean` with a real command line:
--
--   wiz-selfhost check FILE            elaborate and type check; diagnostics, exit 1
--   wiz-selfhost build FILE -o OUT     write the generated C to OUT
--   wiz-selfhost run FILE [ARG…]       compile `main` and run it (also `eval`)
--   wiz-selfhost lsp                   a language server on stdin/stdout (D8: the
--                                      protocol subset `web/selfhost-lsp-shim.js` answers)
--   wiz-selfhost version | help
--   options: -I DIR (module root, repeatable), -o OUT, --cache DIR, --cache-ro DIR
--            (a read-only cache layer, repeatable), --no-cache, --cache-prune DAYS,
--            --cache-verify off|warn|strict, --target c (the backend the host names;
--            llvm/wasm are C5), -v (cache hits/misses), --types (each declaration's type),
--            --trust-native (27a: `def X : a = b := native_refl` is decided by running
--            a and b; the frontend's `Globals.trustNative`), --trust-smt (C15: the `smt`
--            tactic is refused; there is no solver here), --cc, --rt, --cflags,
--            --ldflags (the C toolchain for `run`),
--            --rc | --rc-owned | --gc | --lib | --no-main | --header (the backend),
--            --version, -h | --help. The host's --llvm/--wasm/--split/--cache-ro are
--            recognised and refused with the reason (C5/D5), not as unknown flags.
--   exit codes: 0 ok, 1 user error (no file, the frontend's errors, cc, the program,
--               a bad/unsupported `--target`, a refused `--split`/`--cache-ro`),
--               2 usage (unknown command or option, missing argument)
--
-- Without a subcommand it is the tool it was: `input.wiz` in the working directory to
-- standard output (the fixpoint and the selfhost tests use that), and the first argument
-- may start with `-` (the backend's flags).
--
-- Modules: the frontend's loader (A14, `moduleCheck`) does the work. `import M` is
-- `M.wiz` under each `-I` root in order, then the working directory (dotted names are
-- directories); the root module is `Main`, its path the FILE named. `Prelude` is the
-- embedded prelude and `IO`/`Std`/`Sys` are canonicalised to it. The driver reads the
-- files (`moduleRootSourcesAs`) and names the root; dependencies are elaborated once,
-- before their importers, into the same globals and tables.
--
-- Diagnostics: the frontend reports one line per command, prefixed with the offset of
-- its command (`@N text`, `atLine` in `Frontend.wiz`), and the loader names the module
-- (`@NAME:N text`); the driver turns that into `file:line:col: severity: message [code]`,
-- with the Lean frontend's error code where the message names the same mistake
-- (`ErrorCode.lean`). A stack trace is never printed: every failure is one line, and a
-- missing file is checked with `access` first.
--
-- Cache: `--cache DIR` (default `~/.cache/wiz`) keys an entry by the toolchain id
-- (`toolchainId`, injected by `Wiz/Selfhost.lean` from the selfhost sources and the
-- version), the subcommand's backend flags, the loader's module graph key (every
-- module's name and text, from the graph before elaboration: `keyOfGraph`), the root's
-- `import_c` header texts and the modules' paths. A `.check` entry is the
-- tagged lines and the exit status; a `.c` entry is the C `build` writes (and `run`
-- prints), so a warm build or run skips elaboration and code generation.
--
-- The cache is layered, as the Lean-hosted `wiz`'s is (`Wiz/Cache.lean`, D5):
-- `--cache-ro DIR` (repeatable) adds read-only layers, searched in the order given
-- *after* the writable `--cache`; only `put` and a miss write, so a layer hit is served
-- as it is and never copied back. `--no-cache` clears both lists (a later `--cache` or
-- `--cache-ro` adds one again), so `--no-cache --cache-ro DIR` reads a shared layer and
-- writes nothing. A layer is never created or modified:
-- `--cache-prune DAYS` walks only the write cache and removes the driver's keyed
-- entries (`.check`, `.c`) whose modification time is older than DAYS days; a pruned
-- entry is an ordinary miss, and a layer is never pruned.
--
-- `--cache-verify off|warn|strict` (the host's flag; `require` is `strict`) checks an
-- entry's bytes against an output manifest, `<entry>.mf`: one line, `m<digest>`, the
-- driver's `hashStep` digest (FNV-1a-shaped, modulo 4294967291) of the whole
-- `s<status>\n<payload>` text. The host's
-- manifest is per module (`manifest.d/*.wizmf`, SHA-256 and a Merkle root); the
-- driver's one-file-per-graph cache needs only a digest per entry, and the file names
-- already carry the key. `off` neither reads nor writes manifests, `warn` (the default)
-- verifies one when it exists and otherwise keeps the old unverified lookup, and
-- `strict` uses only manifested entries (a cold strict run writes the manifests, so the
-- next one is warm). Manifests are written to the write cache only, never to a layer.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Options

-- `verify` is `--cache-verify off|warn|strict`, the Lean-hosted `wiz`'s flag (D5);
-- `cacheRo` are the read-only layers, in the order given (`--cache-ro`), and `prune` is
-- `--cache-prune DAYS` (run before the command, never on a layer).
-- `target` is `--target c`, the only backend the self-hosted code generator has (C5).
structure Opts where
  roots : List String
  cache : Option String
  cacheRo : List String
  prune : Option Nat
  out : Option String
  verbose : Bool
  types : Bool
  cc : String
  rt : String
  cflags : List String
  ldflags : List String
  backend : List String
  verify : String
  target : Option String
  -- (27a) `--trust-native`: `native_refl` may decide an equation by running it; the
  -- frontend's `Globals.trustNative` (the host's `Toolchain.trustNative`)
  trustNative : Bool
  -- (C15) the host's `--trust-smt`: accepted, and it selects the `smt` refusal (the
  -- frontend has no solver; see `smtUnsupported`); it is in the cache key when set
  trustSmt : Bool
-- (the cache directory is `$HOME/.cache/wiz` unless `--cache` says otherwise; the
-- `.cache/wiz` here is the fallback for a process without `HOME`, as the host's is)
def optsDefault : Opts :=
  Opts.mk .nil (.some ".cache/wiz") .nil .none .none .false .false "cc" "selfhost" .nil
    .nil .nil "warn" .none .false .false
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The file system (whole-file read and write, directories; `access` is `Backend.wiz`'s
-- `cAccessFails`)

extern "wiz_sys_write_file" cWriteFile : String → String → Nat → IO Nat
-- the Lean-hosted `wiz`'s default cache is `~/.cache/wiz` (`Main.lean`); the driver has
-- the same default. `wiz_sys_getenv` is the Lean runtime's (`runtime/rt_sys.inc`) and
-- the selfhost runtime's (`rt.c`), so the driver builds with either.
extern "wiz_sys_getenv" cGetenv : String → IO String
extern "mkdir" (header := "sys/stat.h") cMkdir : String → Nat → IO Nat
extern "rename" (header := "stdio.h") cRename : String → String → IO Nat
extern "system" (header := "stdlib.h") cSystem : String → IO Nat
-- `--cache-prune` (D5): the host runtime's interfaces (`lib/Sys.wiz`, `Wiz/Cache.lean`);
-- the selfhost runtime has the same three leaves (a list of `kind, size, mtime, ns,
-- mode`; the directory's names; the wall clock).
extern "wiz_sys_list_dir" cListDir : String → IO (List String)
extern "wiz_sys_stat" cStat : String → Bool → IO (List Nat)
extern "wiz_sys_unlink" cUnlink : String → IO Nat
extern "wiz_sys_clock_ns" cClockNs : Nat → IO Nat

-- the default cache directory: `$HOME/.cache/wiz` (the Lean-hosted toolchain's), or
-- `./.cache/wiz` in the working directory when there is no `HOME` (the host reads
-- `$HOME` with `.` as its default too: `Main.lean`)
def defaultCache : IO String :=
  IO.bind (cGetenv "HOME") (fun home => IO.pure (match strEq home "" with
    | .true => "./.cache/wiz"
    | .false => String.append home "/.cache/wiz"))

def pathExists (p : String) : IO Bool :=
  IO.bind (cAccessFails p 0) (fun bad => IO.pure (Bool.not bad))

-- `some`/`none` in `IO ... (Option ...)` need their type written out: inside a bound
-- lambda the frontend has no expected type for a bare constructor (gap A18)
def someIO (t : String) : IO (Option String) := IO.pure (.some t)
def noneIO : IO (Option String) := IO.pure (.none : Option String)

def readIf (p : String) : IO (Option String) :=
  IO.bind (pathExists p) (fun ok => match ok with
    | .false => noneIO
    | .true => IO.bind (IO.readFile p) (fun t => someIO t))

def writeFile (p text : String) : IO Bool :=
  IO.bind (cWriteFile p text 0) (fun st => IO.pure (Nat.beq st 0))

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Strings and lists (the Prelude has few)

def charsOf (s : String) : List Char := match s with
  | .mk cs => cs
def ch (n : Nat) : Char := Char.mk n
def strEqC (c : Char) (n : Nat) : Bool := Nat.beq (Char.code c) n

-- (the compiler source has no `List.map`: the Prelude's is in `preludeText`, for the
-- programs it compiles)
def mapS (f : String → String) : List String → List String
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons s rest => .cons (f s) (mapS f rest)
def mapChars (f : List Char → String) : List (List Char) → List String
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons cs rest => .cons (f cs) (mapChars f rest)

def takeN : List Char → Nat → List Char
  | .nil, _ => .nil
  | _, .zero => .nil
  | .cons c cs, .succ k => .cons c (takeN cs k)

def joinWithNl : List (List Char) → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons l rest => match rest with
    | .nil => l
    | .cons _ _ => List.append l (.cons (ch 10) (joinWithNl rest))

-- the lines of a text, each without its newline (a final newline adds no empty line)
def splitLinesGo : List Char → List Char → List (List Char)
  | .nil, acc => .cons (List.reverseOf acc .nil) .nil
  | .cons c cs, acc => match strEqC c 10 with
    | .true => .cons (List.reverseOf acc .nil) (splitLinesGo cs .nil)
    | .false => splitLinesGo cs (.cons c acc)
def splitLines (s : String) : List (List Char) := match s with
  | .mk cs => match cs with
    | .nil => .nil
    | .cons _ _ => splitLinesGo cs .nil

def charsOfLine : List String → List (List Char)
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons s rest => .cons (charsOf s) (charsOfLine rest)

-- the cache payload of the frontend's lines: one line each, newline-separated
def linesPayload (lines : List String) : String :=
  String.mk (joinWithNl (charsOfLine lines))

-- drop leading spaces
def ltrim : List Char → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons c cs => match strEqC c 32 with
    | .true => ltrim cs
    | .false => .cons c cs

-- the text after `p`, if `p` is its prefix
def stripPrefix (p s : String) : Option String := match p with
  | .mk ps => match s with
    | .mk ss => match dropPrefix ps ss with
      | .some rest => .some (String.mk rest)
      | .none => .none

-- `sub` occurs in `s`
def occursFromSub (pat : List Char) : List Char → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons c cs => match charsPrefix pat (.cons c cs) with
    | .true => .true
    | .false => occursFromSub pat cs
def occursSub (s sub : String) : Bool := match sub with
  | .mk ps => match s with
    | .mk ss => occursFromSub ps ss

-- `A.B` is `A/B.wiz`
def singleton (s : String) : List String := .cons s .nil

def joinSpaces : List String → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .cons s rest => match rest with
    | .nil => s
    | .cons _ _ => String.append s (String.append " " (joinSpaces rest))

def spacesOf : List String → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .cons s rest => String.append " " (String.append s (spacesOf rest))

def docText : Doc → String
  | .t s => s
  | .c a b => String.append (docText a) (docText b)

def docsText : List Doc → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .cons d rest => String.append (docText d) (String.append "\n" (docsText rest))

-- the frontend's output as C comments, before the program (as the one-shot mode prints
-- it, so `-o` is the one-shot output)
def commentLine (l : String) : String := String.append "/* " (String.append l " */")

def commentsOf (lines : List String) : String :=
  match lines with
  | .nil => ""
  | .cons _ _ => String.append (linesPayload (mapS commentLine lines)) "\n"

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Modules and the prepared source

-- a prepared program: the loader's module table (root `Main` last), the run it produced
-- (output lines tagged with their module, globals, tables) and the load order
structure Prepared where
  tab : List ModSrc
  run : Run
  order : List String

-- (`some`/`none` in `IO ... (Option ...)` need their type written out: inside a bound
-- lambda the frontend has no expected type for a bare constructor, gap A18)
def somePrepared (p : Prepared) : IO (Option Prepared) := IO.pure (.some p)
def nonePrepared : IO (Option Prepared) := IO.pure (.none : Option Prepared)

-- the loader's graph before elaboration: the modules and the root's `import_c` headers.
-- A cache lookup needs the key first; `moduleRootSourcesAs` only parses `import` lines,
-- so it is cheap compared with checking the same modules.
structure Graph where
  tab : List ModSrc
  headers : List Header

def someGraph (g : Graph) : IO (Option Graph) := IO.pure (.some g)
def noneGraph : IO (Option Graph) := IO.pure (.none : Option Graph)

-- the frontend's loader (A14): `import M` is `M.wiz` under the `-I` roots, then the
-- working directory; the root module is `Main`, its path the FILE the user named
def loadGraph (roots : List String) (file : String) : IO (Option Graph) :=
  IO.bind (readIf file) (fun t => match t with
    | .none => noneGraph
    | .some text => IO.bind (moduleHeaderTexts text) (fun hs =>
        IO.bind (moduleRootSourcesAs cats tokens roots "Main" file text) (fun tab =>
          someGraph (Graph.mk tab hs))))

-- (27a) `trust` is the run's `--trust-native`: it is handed to the frontend's
-- `Globals.trustNative` (never a property of the source); (C15) `smtTrust` is
-- `--trust-smt`, which selects the `smt` refusal
def runGraph (trust smtTrust : Bool) (g : Graph) : Prepared := match g with
  | .mk tab hs => match modCheckRunHT cats tokens trust smtTrust hs tab (.cons "Main" .nil) with
    | .mk run _ _ order => Prepared.mk tab run order

-- the whole program: the loader, every module checked, and the run it produced
def prepare (trust smtTrust : Bool) (roots : List String) (file : String) : IO (Option Prepared) :=
  IO.bind (loadGraph roots file) (fun g => match g with
    | .none => nonePrepared
    | .some g => somePrepared (runGraph trust smtTrust g))
-- the module `name`'s path (for a diagnostic; the name itself when there is no entry)
def modFile (tab : List ModSrc) (name : String) : String := match modFind tab name with
  | .some (.mk _ p _ _) => match strEq p "" with
    | .true => name
    | .false => p
  | .none => name

def modTextOf (tab : List ModSrc) (name : String) : Option String := match modFind tab name with
  | .some (.mk _ _ t _) => .some t
  | .none => .none

def modTextOr (tab : List ModSrc) (name dflt : String) : String := match modTextOf tab name with
  | .some t => t
  | .none => dflt

-- the load order's module paths, in order (the cache key: a module found under another
-- root is another module for diagnostics)
def modPathsOf (tab : List ModSrc) : List String → List String
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons n ns => .cons (modFile tab n) (modPathsOf tab ns)

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Positions

inductive Pos where
  | mk (line : Nat) (col : Nat)

def lineColGo : List Char → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → Pos
  | .nil, _, _, ln, col => Pos.mk ln col
  | .cons c cs, i, off, ln, col => match Nat.lt i off with
    | .false => Pos.mk ln col
    | .true => match strEqC c 10 with
      | .true => lineColGo cs (Nat.succ i) off (Nat.succ ln) 1
      | .false => lineColGo cs (Nat.succ i) off ln (Nat.succ col)

-- the 1-based line and column of a 0-based offset in a text
def lineCol (text : String) (off : Nat) : Pos := match text with
  | .mk cs => lineColGo cs 0 off 1 1

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Diagnostics

inductive Sev where
  | error
  | warning
  | info
  -- an `info` the Lean-hosted `wiz check` prints without `--types` (`#check`, `#reduce`,
  -- `#eval`); a declaration's own type line waits for `--types` (D6)
  | infoEval

inductive Diag where
  | mk (sev : Sev) (file : String) (line : Nat) (col : Nat) (msg : String) (code : String)

def sevName : Sev → String
  | .error => "error"
  | .warning => "warning"
  | .info => "info"
  | .infoEval => "info"

inductive NumRest where
  | mk (n : Nat) (rest : List Char)

-- the number at the start of `cs`, and the rest
def readNat : List Char → Nat → NumRest
  | .nil, acc => NumRest.mk acc .nil
  | .cons c cs, acc => match isDigitC (Char.code c) with
    | .true => readNat cs (Nat.add (Nat.mul acc 10) (Nat.sub (Char.code c) 48))
    | .false => NumRest.mk acc (.cons c cs)

inductive SplitAt where
  | mk (off : Nat) (text : String)

-- `@OFFSET text` → (offset, text); `(0, l)` for a line without the prefix
def splitAtLine (l : String) : SplitAt := match l with
  | .mk cs => match cs with
    | .nil => SplitAt.mk 0 l
    | .cons c rest => match strEqC c 64 with
      | .false => SplitAt.mk 0 l
      | .true => match rest with
        | .nil => SplitAt.mk 0 l
        | .cons d ds => match isDigitC (Char.code d) with
          | .false => SplitAt.mk 0 l
          | .true => match readNat (.cons d ds) 0 with
            | .mk n after => match after with
              | .cons sp r => match strEqC sp 32 with
                | .true => SplitAt.mk n (String.mk r)
                | .false => SplitAt.mk 0 l
              | .nil => SplitAt.mk 0 l

-- `error 12: expected …` → `expected …` (the parser's message, without its offset)
def afterColonSp : List Char → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .cons c cs => match strEqC c 58 with
    | .true => match cs with
      | .cons _ r => String.mk r
      | .nil => ""
    | .false => String.mk (.cons c cs)

def parseDetail (s : String) : String := match stripPrefix "parse " s with
  | .none => s
  | .some t => match stripPrefix "error " t with
    | .none => s
    | .some u => match u with
      | .mk us => match readNat us 0 with
        | .mk _ after => afterColonSp after

-- the offset a parse error names (`parse error 57: …`): the parser reports the token it
-- stopped at, where the Lean-hosted `wiz` reports it, not the command's start
def parseOff (s : String) : Option Nat := match stripPrefix "parse error " s with
  | .none => .none
  | .some t => match readNat (charsOf t) 0 with
    | .mk n after => match after with
      | .cons c _ => match strEqC c 58 with
        | .true => .some n
        | .false => .none
      | .nil => .none

def sevOf (s : String) : Sev := match stripPrefix "error: " s with
  | .some _ => .error
  | .none => match strStarts "parse error" s with
    | .true => .error
    | .false => match stripPrefix "warning: " s with
      | .some _ => .warning
      | .none => .info

def msgOf (s : String) : String := match stripPrefix "error: " s with
  | .some m => m
  | .none => match strStarts "parse error" s with
    | .true => parseDetail s
    | .false => match stripPrefix "warning: " s with
      | .some m => m
      | .none => s

-- the Lean frontend's code (`ErrorCode.lean`), where the message names the same mistake
-- the Lean frontend's code (`ErrorCode.lean`) for a message, where it names the same
-- mistake: a table of (text, code), in order, then the loader's and the parser's own
inductive CodeEntry where
  | mk (key : String) (code : String)

def codeEntry (m : String) (e : CodeEntry) : Option String := match e with
  | .mk k v => match occursSub m k with
    | .true => .some v
    | .false => .none

def codeLookup (m : String) : List CodeEntry → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .cons e rest => match codeEntry m e with
    | .some v => v
    | .none => codeLookup m rest

def codeTable : List CodeEntry :=
  .cons (.mk "has already been declared" "duplicate-declaration")
  (.cons (.mk "unknown identifier" "unknown-identifier")
  (.cons (.mk "is private to module" "private")
  (.cons (.mk "type mismatch" "type-mismatch")
  (.cons (.mk "no field " "no-such-field")
  (.cons (.mk "cannot infer" "cannot-infer")
  (.cons (.mk "unknown declaration" "unknown-declaration")
  (.cons (.mk "unsupported command " "unknown-syntax")
  (.cons (.mk "unsupported syntax " "unknown-syntax") .nil))))))))

def codeOf (s : String) : String := match stripPrefix "error: " s with
  | .none => match strStarts "parse error" s with
    | .true => "parse-error"
    | .false => ""
  | .some m => match strStarts "cannot find module " m with
    | .true => "unknown-module"
    | .false => match strStarts "import cycle" m with
      | .true => "import-cycle"
      | .false => codeLookup m codeTable

-- a line's tag: the module it came from and its offset in that module's text
inductive Tagged where
  | mk (mod : String) (off : Nat) (text : String)

inductive NameRest where
  | mk (name : List Char) (rest : List Char)

def readToColon : List Char → List Char → NameRest
  | acc, .nil => NameRest.mk .nil .nil
  | acc, .cons c cs => match strEqC c 58 with
    | .true => NameRest.mk (List.reverseOf acc .nil) cs
    | .false => match strEqC c 32 with
      | .true => NameRest.mk .nil .nil
      | .false => readToColon (.cons c acc) cs

-- `@NAME:OFFSET text` (the loader's) or `@OFFSET text` (one file) or no tag
def taggedOf (l : String) : Tagged := match l with
  | .mk cs => match cs with
    | .nil => Tagged.mk "Main" 0 l
    | .cons c rest => match strEqC c 64 with
      | .false => Tagged.mk "Main" 0 l
      | .true => match readToColon .nil rest with
        | .mk name after =>
          let nameStr := String.mk name;
          match strEq nameStr "" with
          | .true => match splitAtLine l with
            | .mk off text => Tagged.mk "Main" off text
          | .false => match readNat after 0 with
            | .mk off afterNum => match afterNum with
              | .cons sp r => match strEqC sp 32 with
                | .true => Tagged.mk nameStr off (String.mk r)
                | .false => Tagged.mk "Main" 0 l
              | .nil => Tagged.mk "Main" 0 l

-- the first `n` characters dropped
def dropChars : Nat → List Char → List Char
  | .zero, cs => cs
  | .succ _, .nil => .nil
  | .succ k, .cons _ cs => dropChars k cs

-- leading whitespace (spaces, tabs, newlines) dropped
def skipSpaceChars : List Char → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons c cs => match strEqC c 32 with
    | .true => skipSpaceChars cs
    | .false => match strEqC c 9 with
      | .true => skipSpaceChars cs
      | .false => match strEqC c 10 with
        | .true => skipSpaceChars cs
        | .false => match strEqC c 13 with
          | .true => skipSpaceChars cs
          | .false => .cons c cs

-- the command that starts at `off`: the first token of the text there
def cmdAt (text : String) (off : Nat) : String := match text with
  | .mk cs => String.mk (skipSpaceChars (dropChars off cs))

-- the characters up to the end of their line
def takeLineChars : List Char → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons c cs => match strEqC c 10 with
    | .true => .nil
    | .false => .cons c (takeLineChars cs)

def dropSpaces : List Char → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons c cs => match strEqC c 32 with
    | .true => dropSpaces cs
    | .false => .cons c cs

-- the characters without their trailing spaces
def rtrimChars (cs : List Char) : List Char :=
  List.reverseOf (dropSpaces (List.reverseOf cs .nil)) .nil

-- (a `#check c` prints `c : T`, as the Lean-hosted `wiz` does; the self-hosted
-- frontend's own line carries the type alone. The source text stands in for the
-- elaborator's pretty-printed term, which the driver has not got.)
def infoPrefix (tab : List ModSrc) (m : String) (off : Nat) : String :=
  match modTextOf tab m with
  | .none => ""
  | .some t => match stripPrefix "#check" (cmdAt t off) with
    | .none => ""
    | .some arg => match rtrimChars (takeLineChars (skipSpaceChars (charsOf arg))) with
      | .nil => ""
      | a => String.append (String.mk a) " : "

-- (`#check c`, `#reduce c` and `#eval c` print their result without `--types`, as the
-- Lean-hosted `wiz check` does; a declaration's own type line does not)
def printsInfo (tab : List ModSrc) (m : String) (off : Nat) : Bool :=
  match modTextOf tab m with
  | .none => .false
  | .some t => match cmdAt t off with
    | s => Bool.or (strStarts "#check" s) (Bool.or (strStarts "#reduce" s) (strStarts "#eval" s))

def sevOfTagged (tab : List ModSrc) (m : String) (off : Nat) (rest : String) : Sev :=
  match sevOf rest with
  | .info => match printsInfo tab m off with
    | .true => .infoEval
    | .false => .info
  | s => s

-- the message: a `#check`'s with the term in front (see `infoPrefix`)
def msgOfTagged (tab : List ModSrc) (m : String) (off : Nat) (rest : String) : String :=
  match sevOf rest with
  | .info => String.append (infoPrefix tab m off) (msgOf rest)
  | _ => msgOf rest

def diagOf (tab : List ModSrc) (l : String) : Diag := match taggedOf l with
  | .mk m off rest =>
    -- a parse error reports the token it stopped at, not its command's start
    let off' := match parseOff rest with
      | .some n => n
      | .none => off;
    match modTextOf tab m with
    | .none => Diag.mk (sevOfTagged tab m off' rest) (modFile tab m) 1 1 (msgOfTagged tab m off' rest) (codeOf rest)
    | .some t => match lineCol t off' with
      | .mk ln col => Diag.mk (sevOfTagged tab m off' rest) (modFile tab m) ln col (msgOfTagged tab m off' rest) (codeOf rest)

def diagsOf (tab : List ModSrc) : List String → List Diag
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons l rest => .cons (diagOf tab l) (diagsOf tab rest)

def hasError : List Diag → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons (.mk sev _ _ _ _ _) rest => match sev with
    | .error => .true
    | _ => hasError rest

def codeSuffix (c : String) : String := match strEq c "" with
  | .true => ""
  | .false => String.append " [" (String.append c "]")

def diagLine (d : Diag) : String := match d with
  | .mk sev f ln col msg code =>
    String.append (String.append f ":") (String.append (Nat.toString ln) (String.append ":"
      (String.append (Nat.toString col) (String.append ": " (String.append (sevName sev)
        (String.append ": " (String.append msg (codeSuffix code))))))))

def emitDiag (o : Opts) (d : Diag) : IO Unit := match d with
  | .mk sev _ _ _ _ _ => match sev with
    | .info => match o.types with
      | .true => IO.println (diagLine d)
      | .false => IO.pure ()
    | .infoEval => IO.println (diagLine d)
    -- (`check` prints a warning, on standard output, as the Lean-hosted `wiz` does)
    | .warning => IO.println (diagLine d)
    | .error => IO.ePrintln (diagLine d)

def emitDiags (o : Opts) : List Diag → IO Unit
  | .nil => IO.pure ()
  | .cons d rest => IO.bind (emitDiag o d) (fun u => emitDiags o rest)

-- `build` and `run` report the errors only (the Lean-hosted `wiz` drops the warnings
-- there: `Main.elabFile`)
def emitErrorOnly (d : Diag) : IO Unit := match d with
  | .mk sev _ _ _ _ _ => match sev with
    | .error => IO.ePrintln (diagLine d)
    | _ => IO.pure ()

def emitErrors : List Diag → IO Unit
  | .nil => IO.pure ()
  | .cons d rest => IO.bind (emitErrorOnly d) (fun u => emitErrors rest)

def ePrintAll : List String → IO Unit
  | .nil => IO.pure ()
  | .cons s ss => IO.bind (IO.ePrintln s) (fun u => ePrintAll ss)

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Directories

def splitSegsGo : List Char → List Char → List (List Char)
  | .nil, acc => .cons (List.reverseOf acc .nil) .nil
  | .cons c cs, acc => match strEqC c 47 with
    | .true => .cons (List.reverseOf acc .nil) (splitSegsGo cs .nil)
    | .false => splitSegsGo cs (.cons c acc)

def splitSegs (p : String) : List (List Char) := match p with
  | .mk cs => splitSegsGo cs .nil

-- make a directory and its parents (`mkdir` errors — an existing one — are ignored)
def mkdirsGo : List (List Char) → String → IO Unit
  | .nil, _ => IO.pure ()
  | .cons seg rest, acc =>
    let s := String.mk seg;
    let acc' := match strEq acc "" with
      | .true => match strEq s "" with
        | .true => "/"
        | .false => s
      | .false => String.append acc (String.append "/" s);
    IO.bind (cMkdir acc' 493) (fun st => mkdirsGo rest acc')

def ensureDir (p : String) : IO Unit := mkdirsGo (splitSegs p) ""

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The cache

def hashStep : List Char → Nat → Nat
  | .nil, h => h
  | .cons c cs, h => hashStep cs (Nat.mod (Nat.add (Nat.mul h 16777619) (Char.code c)) 4294967291)

def hashParts : List String → Nat → Nat
  | .nil, h => h
  | .cons s rest, h => hashParts rest (hashStep (charsOf s) (Nat.mod (Nat.add (Nat.mul h 16777619) 31) 4294967291))

-- the `import_c` headers are read at check time, so their contents belong to the key (a
-- changed header must not be served from a cache entry written for the old one)
def headerHash : List Header → Nat → Nat
  | .nil, h => h
  | .cons (.mk n t) rest, h => headerHash rest (modHash (modHash h n) t)

-- (the cache key) the graph alone: every module's name and text, the paths they were
-- found at, the root's header texts, and the backend flags. This is the same before and
-- after elaboration, so a warm `check`/`run` can answer it without running a command.
-- (27a) `--trust-native` is part of the key, as it is of the host's: a `native_refl`
-- accepted with it is never replayed without it, nor the refusal with it.
def keyOfGraph (o : Opts) (kind : String) (g : Graph) : String := match g with
  | .mk tab hs =>
    let names := tabNames tab;
    let trustPart := match o.trustNative with
      | .true => .cons "--trust-native" .nil
      | .false => (.nil : List String);
    -- (C15) the flag is part of the key when set, as the host's `smtKey` mixes in a
    -- non-default `Smt.Config` (a refusal message is cached with the run that wrote it)
    let smtFlag : List String := match o.trustSmt with
      | .true => .cons "--trust-smt" .nil
      | .false => .nil;
    Nat.toString (hashParts (.cons kind (.cons toolchainId
      (.cons (Nat.toString (moduleGraphKey names tab))
        (.cons (Nat.toString (headerHash hs 17))
          (List.append trustPart (List.append o.backend (List.append smtFlag (modPathsOf tab names)))))))) 2166136261)
def cachePath (dir key ext : String) : String :=
  String.append dir (String.append "/" (String.append key ext))

inductive FirstLine where
  | mk (line : List Char) (rest : String)

def splitFirstLineGo : List Char → List Char → FirstLine
  | .nil, acc => FirstLine.mk (List.reverseOf acc .nil) ""
  | .cons c cs, acc => match strEqC c 10 with
    | .true => FirstLine.mk (List.reverseOf acc .nil) (String.mk cs)
    | .false => splitFirstLineGo cs (.cons c acc)

def splitFirstLine (s : String) : FirstLine := match s with
  | .mk cs => splitFirstLineGo cs .nil

-- a cache entry: `s<status>` on the first line, then the payload. `dir` and `ro` are
-- where the hit came from (a layer hit is never copied into the write cache).
inductive Cached where
  | mk (status : Nat) (payload : String) (dir : String) (ro : Bool)

-- `s12 payload` → the status and the payload
def entryOf (text : String) : Option (Nat × String) := match splitFirstLine text with
  | .mk line payload => match stripPrefix "s" (String.mk line) with
    | .none => .none
    | .some num => match num with
      | .mk ns => match readNat ns 0 with
        | .mk st _ => .some (st, payload)

def entryText (status : Nat) (payload : String) : String :=
  String.append "s" (String.append (Nat.toString status) (String.append "\n" payload))

-- the output manifest: one line, `m<digest>`, over the entry's whole `s<status>` text
-- (`hashStep`, the driver's FNV-1a-shaped rolling hash). The host's manifests are per
-- module and SHA-256 (`Wiz/Cache.lean`); a graph-keyed one-file cache only needs a
-- digest of the bytes it serves (an integrity check, not a signature: the file name
-- already carries the input key).
def entryHash (text : String) : Nat := hashStep (charsOf text) 2166136261

def manifestPath (dir key ext : String) : String :=
  String.append (cachePath dir key ext) ".mf"

def manifestText (text : String) : String :=
  String.append "m" (String.append (Nat.toString (entryHash text)) "\n")

def manifestValue (text : String) : Option Nat := match stripPrefix "m" text with
  | .none => .none
  | .some rest => match readNat (charsOf rest) 0 with
    | .mk n after => match after with
      | .nil => .some n
      | .cons c cs => match strEqC c 10 with
        | .true => match cs with
          | .nil => .some n
          | .cons _ _ => .none
        | .false => .none

-- a cache entry: `s<status>` on the first line, then the payload
def someCached (c : Cached) : IO (Option Cached) := IO.pure (.some c)
def noneCached : IO (Option Cached) := IO.pure (.none : Option Cached)

-- `--cache-verify off|warn|strict` (`require` is the host's synonym for `strict`)
def strictVerify (o : Opts) : Bool :=
  Bool.or (strEq o.verify "strict") (strEq o.verify "require")
def offVerify (o : Opts) : Bool := strEq o.verify "off"

-- one layer: read the entry, then check its manifest when the mode asks for one
def cacheReadAt (o : Opts) (dir key ext : String) (ro : Bool) : IO (Option Cached) :=
  IO.bind (readIf (cachePath dir key ext)) (fun t => match t with
    | .none => noneCached
    | .some text => match entryOf text with
      | .none => noneCached
      | .some (st, payload) => match offVerify o with
        | .true => someCached (Cached.mk st payload dir ro)
        | .false => IO.bind (readIf (manifestPath dir key ext)) (fun m => match m with
          -- (no manifest: `warn` keeps the old lookup, `strict` does not use it)
          | .none => match strictVerify o with
            | .true => noneCached
            | .false => someCached (Cached.mk st payload dir ro)
          | .some mt => match manifestValue mt with
            | .some h => match Nat.beq h (entryHash text) with
              | .true => someCached (Cached.mk st payload dir ro)
              | .false => noneCached
            | .none => match strictVerify o with
              | .true => noneCached
              | .false => someCached (Cached.mk st payload dir ro)))

def cacheReadLayers (o : Opts) (key ext : String) : List String → IO (Option Cached)
  | .nil => noneCached
  | .cons d ds => IO.bind (cacheReadAt o d key ext .true) (fun hit => match hit with
    | .some c => someCached c
    | .none => cacheReadLayers o key ext ds)

-- (the host's order: the write cache first, then the read-only layers in the order given)
def cacheRead (o : Opts) (key ext : String) : IO (Option Cached) := match o.cache with
  | .none => cacheReadLayers o key ext o.cacheRo
  | .some dir => IO.bind (cacheReadAt o dir key ext .false) (fun hit => match hit with
    | .some c => someCached c
    | .none => cacheReadLayers o key ext o.cacheRo)

-- whether there is any cache at all: a write cache or a read-only layer. A read-only-only
-- run still builds the key and reads the layers, and its writes are no-ops.
def cacheOn (o : Opts) : Bool := match o.cache with
  | .some _ => .true
  | .none => match o.cacheRo with
    | .nil => .false
    | .cons _ _ => .true

def cacheWriteDo (o : Opts) (dir key ext : String) (status : Nat) (payload : String) : IO Bool := do
  ensureDir dir;
  let p := cachePath dir key ext;
  let tmp := String.append p ".tmp";
  let text := entryText status payload;
  ok ← writeFile tmp text;
  match ok with
  | .false => IO.pure (Bool.false)
  | .true => do
    st ← cRename tmp p;
    match Nat.beq st 0 with
    | .false => IO.pure (Bool.false)
    | .true => match offVerify o with
      -- (`--cache-verify off`: no manifests are written or read)
      | .true => IO.pure (Bool.true)
      -- (the manifest follows the entry; a failure to write it only loses a strict hit)
      | .false => do
        let mp := manifestPath dir key ext;
        let mtmp := String.append mp ".tmp";
        mok ← writeFile mtmp (manifestText text);
        match mok with
        | .false => IO.pure (Bool.true)
        | .true => do
          st2 ← cRename mtmp mp;
          IO.pure (Bool.true)

-- only the write cache is written: a hit in a layer is returned as it is, never copied
def cacheWrite (o : Opts) (key ext : String) (status : Nat) (payload : String) : IO Bool := match o.cache with
  | .none => IO.pure (Bool.false)
  | .some dir => cacheWriteDo o dir key ext status payload

-- `--no-cache` paths: no key, no read, no write (the caller decides once whether the run
-- is cached, and these keep the cache out of the warm/cold split)
def cacheReadIf (o : Opts) (use : Bool) (key ext : String) : IO (Option Cached) := match use with
  | .true => cacheRead o key ext
  | .false => noneCached

def cacheWriteIf (o : Opts) (use : Bool) (key ext : String) (status : Nat) (payload : String) : IO Bool :=
  match use with
  | .true => cacheWrite o key ext status payload
  | .false => IO.pure (Bool.false)

-- `-v` still says a run was not served from the cache; without a cache there is no key,
-- so the line names the reason instead. A hit names the layer it came from, so a
-- read-only hit is visible (`cache hit: KEY (read-only DIR)`).
def cacheHitMsg (o : Opts) (key : String) (dir : String) (ro : Bool) : IO Unit :=
  if o.verbose then
    match ro with
    | .true => IO.ePrintln (String.append "cache hit: " (String.append key
        (String.append " (read-only " (String.append dir ")"))))
    | .false => IO.ePrintln (String.append "cache hit: " key)
  else IO.pure ()

def cacheMissMsg (o : Opts) (use : Bool) (key : String) : IO Unit := match use with
  | .true => if o.verbose then IO.ePrintln (String.append "cache miss: " key) else IO.pure ()
  | .false => if o.verbose then IO.ePrintln "cache miss: no-cache" else IO.pure ()

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Pruning (`--cache-prune DAYS`)

-- `s` ends with `suf`
def strSuffix (s suf : String) : Bool := match s with
  | .mk ss => match suf with
    | .mk ps => charsPrefix (List.reverseOf ps .nil) (List.reverseOf ss .nil)

-- the whole of `s` is a number (no sign, no trailing characters)
def readNatFull (s : String) : Option Nat := match s with
  | .mk cs => match cs with
    | .nil => .none
    | .cons c _ => match isDigitC (Char.code c) with
      | .false => .none
      | .true => match readNat cs 0 with
        | .mk n rest => match rest with
          | .nil => .some n
          | .cons _ _ => .none

-- the `i`th number (0 when the list is too short)
def pruneNatAt : List Nat → Nat → Nat
  | .nil, _ => 0
  | .cons x xs, .zero => x
  | .cons _ xs, .succ k => pruneNatAt xs k

-- what a prune removed: the driver's two keyed extensions, and their bytes
structure PruneCounts where
  checks : Nat
  programs : Nat
  bytes : Nat

def PruneCounts.total (c : PruneCounts) : Nat := Nat.add c.checks c.programs

def PruneCounts.plus (a b : PruneCounts) : PruneCounts :=
  PruneCounts.mk (Nat.add a.checks b.checks) (Nat.add a.programs b.programs)
    (Nat.add a.bytes b.bytes)

def sizeText (n : Nat) : String := match Nat.lt n 1024 with
  | .true => String.append (Nat.toString n) " B"
  | .false => match Nat.lt n (Nat.mul 1024 1024) with
    | .true => String.append (Nat.toString (Nat.div n 1024)) " KiB"
    | .false => match Nat.lt n (Nat.mul (Nat.mul 1024 1024) 1024) with
      | .true => String.append (Nat.toString (Nat.div n (Nat.mul 1024 1024))) " MiB"
      | .false => String.append (Nat.toString (Nat.div n (Nat.mul (Nat.mul 1024 1024) 1024))) " GiB"

-- the host's `PruneCounts.render`, with the driver's extensions
def pruneRender (c : PruneCounts) (days : Nat) (dir : String) : String :=
  "cache prune: removed " +++ Nat.toString (PruneCounts.total c) +++ " files (" +++
    Nat.toString c.checks +++ " .check, " +++ Nat.toString c.programs +++ " .c), " +++
    sizeText c.bytes +++ " older than " +++ Nat.toString days +++ " days in " +++ dir

inductive Keyed where
  | check
  | program

-- only the driver's keyed entries: a `.mf` manifest, a subdirectory or anything else in
-- the write cache is left alone (the host leaves its manifests too)
def keyedOf (name : String) : Option Keyed := match strSuffix name ".check" with
  | .true => .some Keyed.check
  | .false => match strSuffix name ".c" with
    | .true => .some Keyed.program
    | .false => .none

def addKeyed (k : Keyed) (size : Nat) (c : PruneCounts) : PruneCounts := match k with
  | .check => PruneCounts.mk (Nat.succ c.checks) c.programs (Nat.add c.bytes size)
  | .program => PruneCounts.mk c.checks (Nat.succ c.programs) (Nat.add c.bytes size)

-- one directory's entries: the old keyed files are removed (or counted), and the
-- subdirectories are returned for the walk (links are not followed, as in the host)
inductive PruneStep where
  | mk (counts : PruneCounts) (subdirs : List String)

def pruneNames (dir : String) (cutoff : Nat) : List String → IO PruneStep
  | .nil => IO.pure (PruneStep.mk (PruneCounts.mk 0 0 0) .nil)
  | .cons n rest => do
    tail ← pruneNames dir cutoff rest;
    match tail with
    | .mk c subs => match strEq n "" with
      | .true => IO.pure (PruneStep.mk c subs)
      | .false => do
        let p := String.append dir (String.append "/" n);
        -- (lstat: links are not followed, as the host's pruner does)
        st ← cStat p .false;
        match st with
        | .nil => IO.pure (PruneStep.mk c subs)
        | .cons _ _ => match Nat.beq (pruneNatAt st 0) 1 with
          | .true => IO.pure (PruneStep.mk c (.cons p subs))
          | .false => match Nat.beq (pruneNatAt st 0) 0 with
            | .false => IO.pure (PruneStep.mk c subs)
            | .true => match Nat.lt (pruneNatAt st 2) cutoff with
              | .false => IO.pure (PruneStep.mk c subs)
              | .true => match keyedOf n with
                | .none => IO.pure (PruneStep.mk c subs)
                | .some k => do
                  u ← cUnlink p;
                  IO.pure (PruneStep.mk (addKeyed k (pruneNatAt st 1) c) subs)

-- walk the write cache with a work list; the fuel bounds a pathological tree of
-- directories (a keyed cache is flat, so it is only a safety net)
def pruneWalk (fuel : Nat) (dirs : List String) (cutoff : Nat) : IO PruneCounts :=
  match fuel with
  | .zero => IO.pure (PruneCounts.mk 0 0 0)
  | .succ k => match dirs with
    | .nil => IO.pure (PruneCounts.mk 0 0 0)
    | .cons d rest => do
      names ← cListDir d;
      step ← pruneNames d cutoff names;
      match step with
      | .mk c subs => do
        more ← pruneWalk k (List.append rest subs) cutoff;
        IO.pure (PruneCounts.plus c more)

-- the wall clock as seconds (the host's `Std.Time.Timestamp.now`)
def nowSeconds : IO Nat := IO.bind (cClockNs 1) (fun ns =>
  IO.pure (Nat.div (Nat.div ns 1000000) 1000))

def pruneCache (dir : String) (days : Nat) : IO PruneCounts := do
  now ← nowSeconds;
  let cutoff := Nat.sub now (Nat.mul days 86400);
  pruneWalk 1000000 (.cons dir .nil) cutoff

-- `--cache-prune DAYS`: only the write cache, before the command; with no write cache
-- (or with `--cache-ro` alone) nothing is pruned and nothing is printed
def pruneMaybe (o : Opts) : IO Unit := match o.prune with
  | .none => IO.pure ()
  | .some days => match o.cache with
    | .none => IO.pure ()
    | .some dir => IO.bind (pruneCache dir days) (fun c =>
        IO.ePrintln (pruneRender c days dir))

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The command line

inductive Arg where
  | ok (o : Opts) (file : String) (extra : List String)
  -- a usage error: the message, then the usage hint, exit 2 (the host's `_` case)
  | err (msg : String)
  -- the host's `--target`/`--cache-verify` errors inside its `take*` helpers: the
  -- message alone (no usage), exit 1
  | fail (msg : String)
  | version
  | help

inductive Kind where
  | check
  | build
  | run
  | eval

def isBackendFlag (a : String) : Bool :=
  Bool.or (strEq a "--rc") (Bool.or (strEq a "--rc-owned") (Bool.or (strEq a "--gc")
    (Bool.or (strEq a "--lib") (Bool.or (strEq a "--no-main") (strEq a "--header")))))

-- a word in a list
def listHas (s : String) : List String → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons x rest => match strEq s x with
    | .true => .true
    | .false => listHas s rest

-- `--target`: the host's names are c, llvm and wasm; the self-hosted backend emits C
-- only (C5), so `c` is the one it can select
def targetModes : List String := .cons "c" (.cons "llvm" (.cons "wasm" .nil))

def targetOk (t : String) : Bool := strEq t "c"
def targetKnown (t : String) : Bool := listHas t targetModes

-- `--cache-verify`: the host's modes (`Cache.VerifyMode.ofString?`; `require` is strict)
def verifyOk (m : String) : Bool :=
  Bool.or (strEq m "off") (Bool.or (strEq m "warn") (Bool.or (strEq m "strict") (strEq m "require")))

def verifyErr (m : String) : String :=
  String.append "--cache-verify: unknown mode " (String.append m " (off, warn, strict)")

-- options may come before or after FILE; after FILE, a non-option is a program
-- argument (`run FILE ARG…`), and `--` makes everything after it an argument.
-- The messages match the Lean-hosted `wiz` (`Main.lean`): `unknown flag: X`,
-- `unknown command: …` and exit 2; a value-taking option without its value is an
-- unknown flag there too (its `parseFlags` leaves both words over).
partial def parseOptsGo : List String → Opts → Option String → List String → Arg
  | .nil, o, file, extra => match file with
    | .none => .err "no FILE"
    | .some f => .ok o f (List.reverseOf extra .nil)
  | .cons a rest, o, file, extra => match strEq a "--" with
    | .true => match file with
      | .none => match rest with
        | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --"
        | .cons f r2 => .ok o f r2
      | .some f => .ok o f (List.append (List.reverseOf extra .nil) rest)
    | .false => match strEq a "-I" with
      | .true => match rest with
        | .nil => .err "unknown flag: -I"
        | .cons d r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with roots := List.append o.roots (singleton d) } file extra
      | .false => match strEq a "--include" with
        | .true => match rest with
          | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --include"
          | .cons d r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with roots := List.append o.roots (singleton d) } file extra
        | .false => match strEq a "-o" with
          | .true => match rest with
            | .nil => .err "unknown flag: -o"
            | .cons p r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with out := .some p } file extra
          | .false => match strEq a "--cache" with
            | .true => match rest with
              | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --cache"
              | .cons d r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with cache := .some d } file extra
            | .false => match strEq a "--cache-ro" with
              | .true => match rest with
                | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --cache-ro"
                | .cons d r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with cacheRo := List.append o.cacheRo (singleton d) } file extra
              | .false => match strEq a "--cache-prune" with
                | .true => match rest with
                  | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --cache-prune"
                  | .cons n r2 => match readNatFull n with
                    | .none => .fail (String.append "--cache-prune needs a number of days, not " n)
                    | .some k => match Nat.beq k 0 with
                      | .true => .fail "--cache-prune needs at least one day"
                      | .false => parseOptsGo r2 { o with prune := .some k } file extra
                | .false => match strEq a "--no-cache" with
                  -- (`--no-cache` clears both lists, as the host's does: a later `--cache` or
                  -- `--cache-ro` adds one again)
                  | .true => parseOptsGo rest { o with cache := .none, cacheRo := .nil } file extra
                  | .false => match strEq a "-v" with
                    | .true => parseOptsGo rest { o with verbose := .true } file extra
                    | .false => match strEq a "--verbose" with
                      | .true => parseOptsGo rest { o with verbose := .true } file extra
                      | .false => match strEq a "--types" with
                        | .true => parseOptsGo rest { o with types := .true } file extra
                        | .false => match strEq a "--cc" with
                          | .true => match rest with
                            | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --cc"
                            | .cons c r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with cc := c } file extra
                          | .false => match strEq a "--rt" with
                            | .true => match rest with
                              | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --rt"
                              | .cons d r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with rt := d } file extra
                            | .false => match strEq a "--cflags" with
                              | .true => match rest with
                                | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --cflags"
                                | .cons f r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with cflags := List.append o.cflags (singleton f) } file extra
                              | .false => match strEq a "--ldflags" with
                                | .true => match rest with
                                  | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --ldflags"
                                  | .cons f r2 => parseOptsGo r2 { o with ldflags := List.append o.ldflags (singleton f) } file extra
                                -- (the host's `takeTarget` messages and exit 1)
                                | .false => match strEq a "--target" with
                                  | .true => match rest with
                                    | .nil => .fail "--target needs c, llvm or wasm"
                                    | .cons t r2 => match targetOk t with
                                      | .true => parseOptsGo r2 { o with target := .some t } file extra
                                      | .false => match targetKnown t with
                                        | .true => .fail (String.append "unsupported target " (String.append t ": the self-hosted backend emits C only (C5)"))
                                        | .false => .fail (String.append "unknown target " (String.append t " (choose c, llvm or wasm)"))
                                  | .false => match strEq a "--cache-verify" with
                                    | .true => match rest with
                                      | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --cache-verify"
                                      | .cons m r2 => match verifyOk m with
                                        | .true => parseOptsGo r2 { o with verify := m } file extra
                                        | .false => .err (verifyErr m)
                                    | .false => match stripPrefix "--cache-verify=" a with
                                      | .some m => match verifyOk m with
                                        | .true => parseOptsGo rest { o with verify := m } file extra
                                        | .false => .err (verifyErr m)
                                      | .none => match strEq a "--llvm" with
                                        | .true => .fail "unsupported target llvm: the self-hosted backend emits C only (C5)"
                                        | .false => match strEq a "--wasm" with
                                          | .true => .fail "unsupported target wasm: the self-hosted backend emits C only (C5)"
                                          | .false => match strEq a "--split" with
                                            | .true => match rest with
                                              | .nil => .err "unknown flag: --split"
                                              | .cons n r2 => .fail (String.append "unsupported --split " (String.append n ": the self-hosted backend emits one C unit (C5)"))
                                            | .false => match strEq a "--trust-smt" with
                                              | .true => parseOptsGo rest { o with trustSmt := .true } file extra
                                              | .false => match isBackendFlag a with
                                                | .true => parseOptsGo rest { o with backend := List.append o.backend (singleton a) } file extra
                                                | .false => match strStarts "-" a with
                                                  -- (A14) a root with its directory attached: `-IDIR`,
                                                  -- `-I=DIR`, `--include=DIR` (the loader's `modRoots`)
                                                  | .true => match modAttachedRoot a with
                                                    | .some d => parseOptsGo rest { o with roots := List.append o.roots (singleton d) } file extra
                                                    -- (27a) the host's `--trust-native`: a switch,
                                                    -- before or after the command, as in its
                                                    -- `parseFlags` (the value form is not one: the
                                                    -- host leaves `--trust-native=…` over as an
                                                    -- unknown flag, and so does this)
                                                    | .none => match strEq a "--trust-native" with
                                                      | .true => parseOptsGo rest { o with trustNative := .true } file extra
                                                      | .false => .err (String.append "unknown flag: " a)
                                                  | .false => match file with
                                                    | .none => parseOptsGo rest o (.some a) extra
                                                    | .some _ => parseOptsGo rest o file (.cons a extra)
def parseOpts (args : List String) (o : Opts) : Arg := parseOptsGo args o .none .nil

def usageText : String :=
  "usage: wiz-selfhost COMMAND FILE [OPTIONS]\n" +++
  "\n" +++
  "  wiz-selfhost check FILE         elaborate and type check FILE (diagnostics on\n" +++
  "                                  standard error; exit 1 if it has errors)\n" +++
  "  wiz-selfhost build FILE -o OUT  write the generated C to OUT\n" +++
  "  wiz-selfhost run FILE [ARG]...  compile `main` and run it (also `eval`)\n" +++
  "  wiz-selfhost version            print the version (also --version)\n" +++
  "  wiz-selfhost help               this text (also -h, --help)\n" +++
  "  wiz-selfhost lsp                a language server on stdin/stdout: initialize,\n" +++
  "                                  full-text didOpen/didChange/didClose,\n" +++
  "                                  publishDiagnostics, plainGoal/plainTermGoal (D8)\n" +++
  "\n" +++
  "options: -I DIR (a module root, repeatable; an `import M` is M.wiz there, then\n" +++
  "  in the working directory),\n" +++
  "  -o OUT (the C `run` compiles, kept), --cache DIR (default ~/.cache/wiz, as\n" +++
  "  the Lean-hosted `wiz`'s), --cache-ro DIR (a read-only layer, repeatable:\n" +++
  "  searched after --cache in order, never written), --no-cache (both lists),\n" +++
  "  --cache-prune DAYS (remove the write cache's keyed entries older than DAYS\n" +++
  "  days before the command; a layer is never pruned),\n" +++
  "  --cache-verify off|warn|strict (check an entry against its output manifest;\n" +++
  "  strict: only manifested entries), --target c (the only backend;\n" +++
  "  --llvm/--wasm/--split are the host's and are refused, C5),\n" +++
  "  -v (cache hits and misses), --types (each declaration's type),\n" +++
  "  --trust-native (27a: `def X : a = b := native_refl` is decided by running a and\n" +++
  "  b, not by the kernel; `#print axioms` lists the axiom it adds. There is no\n" +++
  "  --native-fuel: the self-hosted evaluator has no step counter),\n" +++
  "  --cc CMD, --rt DIR (the selfhost runtime, default selfhost), --cflags FLAGS,\n" +++
  "  --ldflags FLAGS, --trust-smt (the `smt` tactic is refused: no solver here, C15);\n" +++
  "  backend: --rc, --rc-owned, --gc, --lib, --no-main, --header\n" +++
  "\n" +++
  "without a command: input.wiz in the working directory to standard output\n"

def versionText : String := String.append "wiz-selfhost " wizVersion

-- the Lean-hosted `wiz`'s usage errors: the message, then the usage, exit 2
def usageError (msg : String) : IO Unit := do
  IO.ePrintln msg;
  IO.ePrintln usageText;
  Process.exit 2

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- check

def statusOf (ds : List Diag) : Nat := match hasError ds with
  | .true => 1
  | .false => 0

def linesOf (r : Run) : List String := List.reverseOf (Run.out r) .nil

def checkGraph (o : Opts) (g : Graph) : IO Unit := match g with
  | .mk tab _ => match cacheOn o with
    -- no cache: do not even build the key (it hashes every module's text)
    | .false => do
      cacheMissMsg o .false "";
      let p := runGraph o.trustNative o.trustSmt g;
      let ds := diagsOf p.tab (linesOf p.run);
      let st := statusOf ds;
      emitDiags o ds;
      match Nat.beq st 0 with
      | .true => IO.pure ()
      | .false => Process.exit 1
    | .true => do
      let key := keyOfGraph o "check" g;
      cached ← cacheRead o key ".check";
      match cached with
      | .some (.mk st payload from ro) => do
        cacheHitMsg o key from ro;
        let ds := diagsOf tab (mapChars (fun cs => String.mk cs) (splitLines payload));
        emitDiags o ds;
        match Nat.beq st 0 with
        | .true => IO.pure ()
        | .false => Process.exit 1
      | .none => do
        if o.verbose then IO.ePrintln (String.append "cache miss: " key) else IO.pure ();
        let p := runGraph o.trustNative o.trustSmt g;
        let lines := linesOf p.run;
        let ds := diagsOf p.tab lines;
        let st := statusOf ds;
        cacheWrite o key ".check" st (linesPayload lines);
        emitDiags o ds;
        match Nat.beq st 0 with
        | .true => IO.pure ()
        | .false => Process.exit 1

def missingFile (file : String) : IO Unit := do
  IO.ePrintln (diagLine (Diag.mk .error file 1 1 "no such file" ""));
  Process.exit 1

def checkCmd (o : Opts) (file : String) : IO Unit := do
  gopt ← loadGraph o.roots file;
  match gopt with
  | .none => missingFile file
  | .some g => checkGraph o g

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- build: the C, to OUT

def cOf (o : Opts) (p : Prepared) : IO (Option String) := do
  let lines := linesOf p.run;
  let ds := diagsOf p.tab lines;
  match hasError ds with
  | .true => IO.bind (emitErrors ds) (fun u => noneIO)
  | .false => IO.bind (missingLinks (List.reverseOf (Globals.ffi (Run.gs p.run)) .nil)) (fun missing => match missing with
    | .cons _ _ => IO.bind (ePrintAll missing) (fun u => noneIO)
    | .nil => someIO (String.append (commentsOf (mapS (fun l => stripAt l) lines))
        (docsText (genProgramArgs o.backend (modTextOr p.tab "Main" "") (Run.gs p.run)))))

def writeOut (out text : String) : IO Unit := do
  ok ← writeFile out text;
  match ok with
  | .true => IO.pure ()
  | .false => do IO.ePrintln (String.append "error: cannot write " out); Process.exit 1

-- the C for `p`, through the cache: `build` and `run` share the `.c` entry (the key
-- covers the backend flags), so a second build is a hit, as the Lean-hosted `wiz`'s is.
-- The key is the graph's (`keyOfGraph`), so a hit skips elaboration; a miss, or
-- `--no-cache` (no key at all), elaborates.
def buildMiss (o : Opts) (useCache : Bool) (cKey checkKey : String) (out : String) (p : Prepared) : IO Unit := do
  c ← cOf o p;
  match c with
  | .none => Process.exit 1
  | .some ctext => do
    cacheWriteIf o useCache checkKey ".check" 0 (linesPayload (linesOf p.run));
    cacheWriteIf o useCache cKey ".c" 0 ctext;
    writeOut out ctext

def buildWith (o : Opts) (out : String) (g : Graph) : IO Unit := match cacheOn o with
  | .false => do
    cacheMissMsg o .false "";
    buildMiss o .false "" "" out (runGraph o.trustNative o.trustSmt g)
  | .true => do
    let key := keyOfGraph o "c" g;
    cached ← cacheRead o key ".c";
    match cached with
    | .some (.mk st ctext from ro) => do
      cacheHitMsg o key from ro;
      writeOut out ctext
    | .none => do
      cacheMissMsg o .true key;
      buildMiss o .true key (keyOfGraph o "check" g) out (runGraph o.trustNative o.trustSmt g)

def buildCmd (o : Opts) (file : String) : IO Unit :=
  match o.out with
  | .none => usageError "build needs -o OUT"
  | .some out => do
    gopt ← loadGraph o.roots file;
    match gopt with
    | .none => missingFile file
    | .some g => buildWith o out g

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- run / eval

def ccCommand (o : Opts) (src prog : String) : String :=
  String.append o.cc (String.append " -O2 -w -I" (String.append o.rt (String.append (spacesOf o.cflags)
    (String.append " " (String.append src (String.append " -o " (String.append prog (spacesOf o.ldflags))))))))

def exitCodeOf (st : Nat) : Nat := Nat.div st 256

def compileAndRun (o : Opts) (key : String) (ctext : String) (extra : List String) : IO Unit := do
  let dir := String.append "/tmp/wiz-selfhost-" key;
  ensureDir dir;
  let src := String.append dir "/main.c";
  ok ← writeFile src ctext;
  match ok with
  | .false => do IO.ePrintln (String.append "error: cannot write " src); Process.exit 1
  | .true => do
    match o.out with
    | .some p => do kept ← writeFile p ctext; IO.pure ()
    | .none => IO.pure ();
    let prog := String.append dir "/prog";
    let cmd := ccCommand o src prog;
    st ← cSystem cmd;
    match Nat.beq st 0 with
    | .false => do
      IO.ePrintln (String.append "error: the C compiler failed (the C is " (String.append src "):"));
      IO.ePrintln cmd;
      Process.exit 1
    | .true => do
      st2 ← cSystem (String.append prog (spacesOf extra));
      match Nat.beq (exitCodeOf st2) 0 with
      | .true => IO.pure ()
      | .false => do
        IO.ePrintln (String.append "error: the program exited with code " (Nat.toString (exitCodeOf st2)));
        Process.exit 1

def runPrepared (o : Opts) (useCache : Bool) (cKey checkKey : String) (p : Prepared)
    (extra : List String) : IO Unit := do
  cached ← cacheReadIf o useCache cKey ".c";
  match cached with
  | .some (.mk st ctext from ro) => do
    cacheHitMsg o cKey from ro;
    compileAndRun o cKey ctext extra
  | .none => do
    cacheMissMsg o useCache cKey;
    let lines := linesOf p.run;
    let ds := diagsOf p.tab lines;
    let st := statusOf ds;
    cacheWriteIf o useCache checkKey ".check" st (linesPayload lines);
    match Nat.beq st 0 with
    | .false => do emitErrors ds; Process.exit 1
    | .true => do
      missing ← missingLinks (List.reverseOf (Globals.ffi (Run.gs p.run)) .nil);
      match missing with
      | .cons _ _ => do ePrintAll missing; Process.exit 1
      | .nil => do
        let ctext := String.append (commentsOf (mapS (fun l => stripAt l) lines))
          (docsText (genProgramArgs o.backend (modTextOr p.tab "Main" "") (Run.gs p.run)));
        cacheWriteIf o useCache cKey ".c" 0 ctext;
        compileAndRun o cKey ctext extra

def runCmd (o : Opts) (file : String) (extra : List String) : IO Unit := do
  gopt ← loadGraph o.roots file;
  match gopt with
  | .none => missingFile file
  | .some g => match cacheOn o with
    | .false => runPrepared o .false "nocache" "" (runGraph o.trustNative o.trustSmt g) extra
    | .true => do
      let cKey := keyOfGraph o "c" g;
      cached ← cacheRead o cKey ".c";
      match cached with
      | .some (.mk st ctext from ro) => do
        cacheHitMsg o cKey from ro;
        compileAndRun o cKey ctext extra
      | .none => runPrepared o .true cKey (keyOfGraph o "check" g) (runGraph o.trustNative o.trustSmt g) extra

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- the one-shot mode: input.wiz → standard output (the fixpoint and the tests), the
-- module loader with `-I` roots and the embedded Prelude

def commentLines : List String → List String
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons l rest => .cons (String.append "/* " (String.append l " */")) (commentLines rest)

def errLines : List String → List String
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons l rest => match strStarts "error" (stripAt l) with
    | .true => .cons (stripAt l) (errLines rest)
    | .false => errLines rest

def legacyFinish (args : List String) (text : String) (lines : List String) (gs : Globals) : IO Unit := do
  missing ← missingLinks (List.reverseOf (Globals.ffi gs) .nil);
  match List.append (errLines lines) missing with
  | .nil => do
    printAll (commentLines (mapS (fun l => stripAt l) lines));
    printDocs (genProgramArgs args text gs)
  | .cons e es => do
    ePrintAll (.cons e es);
    Process.exit 1

def legacyCmd (args : List String) : IO Unit := do
  text ← IO.readFile "input.wiz";
  hs ← moduleHeaderTexts text;
  tab ← moduleRootSources cats tokens (modRoots args) text;
  -- (27a) the one-shot mode reads `--trust-native` too (the frontend's
  -- `Globals.trustNative`; `genProgramArgs` ignores the flag itself); (C15) it reads
  -- `--trust-smt` as well (the `smt` refusal)
  match modCheckRunHT cats tokens (listHas "--trust-native" args) (modHasFlag args "--trust-smt") hs tab (.cons "Main" .nil) with
  | .mk run _ _ _ => legacyFinish args text (linesOf run) (Run.gs run)

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- lsp: the language server (D8), JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout
--
-- The subset is the one the playground's self-hosted shim answers
-- (`web/selfhost-lsp-shim.js`, the `docs/playground-lsp.md` contract): `initialize`
-- (`textDocumentSync` 1: full text, `wizInfoview` v1), `textDocument/didOpen`,
-- `didChange`, `didClose`, `textDocument/publishDiagnostics`, the `wiz/elaborated`
-- notification when the client asks for it, and the infoview's plain queries
-- (`wiz/plainGoal`, `wiz/plainTermGoal`): a check with the collection on records each
-- definition body's expected type and, in a `by` block, the goals after each tactic
-- (`LspEntry` in `selfhost/Frontend.wiz`), and the queries answer from those entries in
-- the host's shapes (`Wiz/LSP.lean`): `plainTermGoal` is `{goal, range}` of the
-- innermost term at the cursor, `plainGoal` the nearest snapshot at or before it
-- (`{rendered, goals, messages}`, `null` outside every `by` block). `textDocument/hover`
-- is `null` and the interactive infoview methods are `MethodNotFound`, as in the shim.
-- Diagnostics are `check`'s, with `source: "wiz"`,
-- the code `check` prints, and a range from the diagnostic's position to the end of its
-- line. An imported module's diagnostics are not published: open that module. A
-- document's URI need not name a file (the playground's is `file:///playground-*.wiz`):
-- the text is the buffer's, and the path only names it in diagnostics and is the first
-- `import` root. (`import_c` headers are read from the server's working directory, as
-- `check` reads them; the Lean server resolves them beside the document.) Positions are
-- the frontend's, which count characters; as in the Lean server (`Wiz/LSP.lean`), that
-- agrees with LSP's UTF-16 unit outside the BMP.
--
-- Not here (see `wiz-notes/selfhost-parity.md` D8): definition, references,
-- completion, signature help, inlay hints, semantic tokens, document and workspace
-- symbols, folding, code actions, formatting (`fmt`), the documentation generator
-- (`doc`), and `repl`.

-- one byte of the client's stream. `getchar` is C's `int`; the return is read as
-- `UInt64`, so the end of the file (a negative `int`, hence above any byte) is seen
-- before `UInt64.toNat`, which would refuse 2^64-1 (a `Nat` is 63 bits here)
extern "getchar" (header := "stdio.h") cGetchar : IO UInt64

-- (`lspSomeNat`/…: inside a bound lambda the frontend has no expected type for a bare
-- constructor, gap A18; a helper gives it one from its signature)
def lspSomeNat (n : Nat) : Option Nat := .some n
def lspNoneNat : Option Nat := .none
def lspSomeStr (s : String) : Option String := .some s
def lspNoneStr : Option String := .none

def lspByte : IO (Option Nat) := IO.bind cGetchar (fun c =>
  match UInt64.lt c (UInt64.ofNat 256) with
  | .true => IO.pure (lspSomeNat (UInt64.toNat c))
  | .false => IO.pure lspNoneNat)

-- ## JSON (RFC 8259, the subset the messages need)

-- a parsed value (or key) and the characters left (a structure: a pair `×` here is a
-- sigma, whose `Prod` name is not in scope in this source)
structure JRes (A : Type) where
  val : A
  rest : List Char

mutual
inductive J where
  | jnull
  | jbool (b : Bool)
  | jnum (text : String)
  | jstr (s : String)
  | jarr (xs : JList)
  | jobj (fs : JObj)
inductive JList where
  | jnil
  | jcons (head : J) (tail : JList)
inductive JObj where
  | onil
  | ocons (key : String) (val : J) (tail : JObj)
end

def jAppend : JList → JList → JList
  | .jnil, ys => ys
  | .jcons h t, ys => .jcons h (jAppend t ys)

def oAppend : JObj → JObj → JObj
  | .onil, ys => ys
  | .ocons k v t, ys => .ocons k v (oAppend t ys)

def jReverse : JList → JList
  | .jnil => .jnil
  | .jcons h t => jAppend (jReverse t) (.jcons h .jnil)

def oReverse : JObj → JObj
  | .onil => .onil
  | .ocons k v t => oAppend (oReverse t) (.ocons k v .onil)

def jDigit (c : Char) : Bool :=
  let n := Char.code c;
  Bool.and (Nat.le 48 n) (Nat.le n 57)

def jSpace (c : Char) : Bool :=
  let n := Char.code c;
  Bool.or (Nat.beq n 32) (Bool.or (Nat.beq n 10) (Bool.or (Nat.beq n 13) (Nat.beq n 9)))

def jSkip : List Char → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons c cs => match jSpace c with
    | .true => jSkip cs
    | .false => .cons c cs

def jHexChar (c : Char) : Bool :=
  let n := Char.code c;
  Bool.or (Bool.and (Nat.le 48 n) (Nat.le n 57))
    (Bool.or (Bool.and (Nat.le 65 n) (Nat.le n 70)) (Bool.and (Nat.le 97 n) (Nat.le n 102)))

def jHexNum (c : Char) : Nat :=
  let n := Char.code c;
  if Bool.and (Nat.le 48 n) (Nat.le n 57) then Nat.sub n 48 else
  if Bool.and (Nat.le 65 n) (Nat.le n 70) then Nat.sub n 55 else
  if Bool.and (Nat.le 97 n) (Nat.le n 102) then Nat.sub n 87 else 0

-- four hex digits after `\u`, as a number and the rest
def jHex4 : Nat → List Char → Option (JRes Nat)
  | .zero, cs => .some (JRes.mk 0 cs)
  | .succ k, cs => match cs with
    | .nil => .none
    | .cons c rest => match jHexChar c with
      | .false => .none
      | .true => match jHex4 k rest with
        | .none => .none
        | .some (JRes.mk acc r) =>
          .some (JRes.mk (Nat.add (Nat.mul (jHexNum c) (Nat.pow 16 k)) acc) r)

-- a `\uXXXX` code unit and the rest: a high surrogate followed by a low one is one
-- code point (as `lib/Json.wiz`'s parser does)
def jCodePoint (cp : Nat) (rest : List Char) : JRes Nat :=
  if Bool.and (Nat.le 0xD800 cp) (Nat.le cp 0xDBFF) then (match rest with
    | .cons b (.cons u (.cons d ds)) =>
      if Bool.and (Nat.beq (Char.code b) 92) (Nat.beq (Char.code u) 117) then (match jHex4 4 (.cons d ds) with
        | .some (JRes.mk lo r) =>
          if Bool.and (Nat.le 0xDC00 lo) (Nat.le lo 0xDFFF) then
            JRes.mk (Nat.add 0x10000 (Nat.add (Nat.mul (Nat.sub cp 0xD800) 1024) (Nat.sub lo 0xDC00))) r
          else JRes.mk cp rest
        | .none => JRes.mk cp rest)
      else JRes.mk cp rest
    | _ => JRes.mk cp rest)
  else JRes.mk cp rest

-- the characters of a string literal after its opening quote, reversed in `acc`
partial def jStringGo : List Char → List Char → Option (JRes String)
  | .nil, _ => .none
  | .cons c cs, acc =>
    let n := Char.code c;
    if Nat.beq n 34 then .some (JRes.mk (String.mk (List.reverseOf acc .nil)) cs) else
    if Nat.beq n 92 then (match cs with
      | .nil => .none
      | .cons e rest =>
        let m := Char.code e;
        if Nat.beq m 110 then jStringGo rest (.cons (Char.mk 10) acc) else
        if Nat.beq m 116 then jStringGo rest (.cons (Char.mk 9) acc) else
        if Nat.beq m 114 then jStringGo rest (.cons (Char.mk 13) acc) else
        if Nat.beq m 98 then jStringGo rest (.cons (Char.mk 8) acc) else
        if Nat.beq m 102 then jStringGo rest (.cons (Char.mk 12) acc) else
        if Nat.beq m 117 then (match jHex4 4 rest with
          | .none => .none
          | .some (JRes.mk cp r) => let p := jCodePoint cp r; jStringGo p.rest (.cons (Char.mk p.val) acc))
        else jStringGo rest (.cons e acc))
    else jStringGo cs (.cons c acc)

def jNumChar (c : Char) : Bool :=
  let n := Char.code c;
  Bool.or (jDigit c) (Bool.or (Nat.beq n 45) (Bool.or (Nat.beq n 43) (Bool.or (Nat.beq n 46)
    (Bool.or (Nat.beq n 101) (Nat.beq n 69)))))

def jNumberGo : List Char → List Char → JRes String
  | .nil, acc => JRes.mk (String.mk (List.reverseOf acc .nil)) .nil
  | .cons c cs, acc => match jNumChar c with
    | .true => jNumberGo cs (.cons c acc)
    | .false => JRes.mk (String.mk (List.reverseOf acc .nil)) (.cons c cs)

mutual
partial def jValue (cs : List Char) : Option (JRes J) := match jSkip cs with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons c rest =>
    let n := Char.code c;
    if Nat.beq n 123 then jObject rest else
    if Nat.beq n 91 then jArray rest else
    if Nat.beq n 34 then (match jStringGo rest .nil with
      | .some (JRes.mk s r) => .some (JRes.mk (.jstr s) r)
      | .none => .none)
    else if Nat.beq n 116 then jLiteral "true" (.jbool .true) (.cons c rest)
    else if Nat.beq n 102 then jLiteral "false" (.jbool .false) (.cons c rest)
    else if Nat.beq n 110 then jLiteral "null" .jnull (.cons c rest)
    else if jNumChar c then (let r := jNumberGo (.cons c rest) .nil;
      .some (JRes.mk (.jnum r.val) r.rest))
    else .none

partial def jLiteral (w : String) (v : J) (cs : List Char) : Option (JRes J) :=
  match stripPrefix w (String.mk cs) with
  | .some rest => .some (JRes.mk v (charsOf rest))
  | .none => .none

partial def jArray (cs : List Char) : Option (JRes J) := match jSkip cs with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons c rest =>
    if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 93 then .some (JRes.mk (.jarr .jnil) rest)
    else (match jValue (.cons c rest) with
      | .none => .none
      | .some (JRes.mk v r) => jArrayMore (.jcons v .jnil) r)

partial def jArrayMore (acc : JList) (cs : List Char) : Option (JRes J) := match jSkip cs with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons c rest =>
    if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 44 then (match jValue rest with
      | .none => .none
      | .some (JRes.mk v r) => jArrayMore (.jcons v acc) r)
    else if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 93 then .some (JRes.mk (.jarr (jReverse acc)) rest)
    else .none

partial def jKey (cs : List Char) : Option (JRes String) := match jSkip cs with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons c rest =>
    if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 34 then (match jStringGo rest .nil with
      | .some (JRes.mk s r) => .some (JRes.mk s r)
      | .none => .none)
    else .none

partial def jColon (cs : List Char) : Option (List Char) := match jSkip cs with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons c rest => if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 58 then .some rest else .none

partial def jObject (cs : List Char) : Option (JRes J) := match jSkip cs with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons c rest =>
    if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 125 then .some (JRes.mk (.jobj .onil) rest)
    else (match jKey (.cons c rest) with
      | .none => .none
      | .some (JRes.mk k r) => (match jColon r with
        | .none => .none
        | .some r2 => (match jValue r2 with
          | .none => .none
          | .some (JRes.mk v r3) => jObjectMore (.ocons k v .onil) r3)))

partial def jObjectMore (acc : JObj) (cs : List Char) : Option (JRes J) := match jSkip cs with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons c rest =>
    if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 44 then (match jKey rest with
      | .none => .none
      | .some (JRes.mk k r) => (match jColon r with
        | .none => .none
        | .some r2 => (match jValue r2 with
          | .none => .none
          | .some (JRes.mk v r3) => jObjectMore (.ocons k v acc) r3)))
    else if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 125 then .some (JRes.mk (.jobj (oReverse acc)) rest)
    else .none
end

def jHexDigit (d : Nat) : Char := if Nat.lt d 10 then Char.mk (Nat.add 48 d) else Char.mk (Nat.add 87 d)

def jEscape (n : Nat) : List Char :=
  if Nat.beq n 34 then .cons (Char.mk 92) (.cons (Char.mk 34) .nil) else
  if Nat.beq n 92 then .cons (Char.mk 92) (.cons (Char.mk 92) .nil) else
  if Nat.beq n 10 then .cons (Char.mk 92) (.cons (Char.mk 110) .nil) else
  if Nat.beq n 13 then .cons (Char.mk 92) (.cons (Char.mk 114) .nil) else
  if Nat.beq n 9 then .cons (Char.mk 92) (.cons (Char.mk 116) .nil) else
  if Nat.lt n 32 then
    .cons (Char.mk 92) (.cons (Char.mk 117) (.cons (Char.mk 48) (.cons (Char.mk 48)
      (.cons (jHexDigit (Nat.div n 16)) (.cons (jHexDigit (Nat.mod n 16)) .nil)))))
  else .cons (Char.mk n) .nil

def jQuoteChars : List Char → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons c cs => List.append (jEscape (Char.code c)) (jQuoteChars cs)

def jQuote (s : String) : String := match s with
  | .mk cs => String.mk (.cons (Char.mk 34) (List.append (jQuoteChars cs) (.cons (Char.mk 34) .nil)))

mutual
partial def jRender : J → String
  | .jnull => "null"
  | .jbool b => if b then "true" else "false"
  | .jnum t => t
  | .jstr s => jQuote s
  | .jarr xs => String.append "[" (String.append (jRenderList xs) "]")
  | .jobj fs => String.append "{" (String.append (jRenderObj fs) "}")

partial def jRenderList : JList → String
  | .jnil => ""
  | .jcons h .jnil => jRender h
  | .jcons h t => String.append (jRender h) (String.append "," (jRenderList t))

partial def jRenderObj : JObj → String
  | .onil => ""
  | .ocons k v .onil => String.append (jQuote k) (String.append ":" (jRender v))
  | .ocons k v t => String.append (jQuote k) (String.append ":" (String.append (jRender v)
      (String.append "," (jRenderObj t))))
end

def someJ (j : J) : Option J := .some j
def noneJ : Option J := .none

-- a field of an object, or `none`
def jField (fs : JObj) (key : String) : Option J := match fs with
  | .onil => .none
  | .ocons k v t => if strEq k key then .some v else jField t key

-- a field of a value, when it is an object
def jGet (o : Option J) (key : String) : Option J := match o with
  | .some (.jobj fs) => jField fs key
  | _ => .none

partial def jAt (j : J) (path : List String) : Option J := match path with
  | .nil => .some j
  | .cons k rest => match jGet (.some j) k with
    | .some v => jAt v rest
    | .none => .none

def jStrOf (o : Option J) : String := match o with
  | .some (.jstr s) => s
  | _ => ""

def jNatOf (o : Option J) : Nat := match o with
  | .some (.jnum t) => match readNat (charsOf t) 0 with
    | .mk n _ => n
  | _ => 0

def jIsTrue (o : Option J) : Bool := match o with
  | .some (.jbool .true) => .true
  | _ => .false

-- ## Framing (`Content-Length` counts UTF-8 bytes, the header a blank line)

def lspDropCr : List Char → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons c cs => if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 13 then cs else .cons c cs

-- the line `acc` (reversed) so far, as text
def lspLine (acc : List Char) : Option String := match acc with
  | .nil => lspNoneStr
  | .cons _ _ => lspSomeStr (String.mk (List.reverseOf (lspDropCr acc) .nil))

partial def lspReadLine (acc : List Char) : IO (Option String) :=
  IO.bind lspByte (fun b => match b with
    | .none => IO.pure (lspLine acc)
    | .some n => if Nat.beq n 10 then IO.pure (lspLine acc)
        else lspReadLine (.cons (Char.mk n) acc))

-- the body's bytes, reversed (a list, not `Bytes`: the embedded prelude's `push` is a
-- list append, so a body read byte by byte would be quadratic there)
partial def lspReadBytes : Nat → List Nat → IO (List Nat)
  | .zero, acc => IO.pure acc
  | .succ k, acc => IO.bind lspByte (fun b => match b with
    | .none => IO.pure acc
    | .some n => lspReadBytes k (.cons n acc))

-- UTF-8 (RFC 3629) as text; a malformed sequence drops its lead byte
partial def lspUtf8 : List Nat → List Char
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons b bs =>
    if Nat.lt b 128 then .cons (Char.mk b) (lspUtf8 bs) else
    if Bool.and (Nat.le 194 b) (Nat.le b 223) then (match bs with
      | .cons b2 r => if Bool.and (Nat.le 128 b2) (Nat.le b2 191) then
          .cons (Char.mk (Nat.add (Nat.mul (Nat.sub b 192) 64) (Nat.sub b2 128))) (lspUtf8 r)
        else lspUtf8 bs
      | .nil => .nil)
    else if Bool.and (Nat.le 224 b) (Nat.le b 239) then (match bs with
      | .cons b2 (.cons b3 r) =>
        if Bool.and (Nat.le 128 b2) (Bool.and (Nat.le b2 191) (Bool.and (Nat.le 128 b3) (Nat.le b3 191))) then
          .cons (Char.mk (Nat.add (Nat.mul (Nat.sub b 224) 4096)
            (Nat.add (Nat.mul (Nat.sub b2 128) 64) (Nat.sub b3 128)))) (lspUtf8 r)
        else lspUtf8 bs
      | _ => .nil)
    else if Bool.and (Nat.le 240 b) (Nat.le b 244) then (match bs with
      | .cons b2 (.cons b3 (.cons b4 r)) =>
        if Bool.and (Bool.and (Nat.le 128 b2) (Nat.le b2 191)) (Bool.and (Nat.le 128 b3)
            (Bool.and (Nat.le b3 191) (Bool.and (Nat.le 128 b4) (Nat.le b4 191)))) then
          .cons (Char.mk (Nat.add (Nat.mul (Nat.sub b 240) 262144) (Nat.add (Nat.mul (Nat.sub b2 128) 4096)
            (Nat.add (Nat.mul (Nat.sub b3 128) 64) (Nat.sub b4 128))))) (lspUtf8 r)
        else lspUtf8 bs
      | _ => .nil)
    else lspUtf8 bs

def lspFromBytes (bs : List Nat) : String := String.mk (lspUtf8 bs)

-- the UTF-8 bytes of one code point
def lspUtf8Bytes (c : Nat) : List Nat :=
  if Nat.lt c 128 then .cons c .nil else
  if Nat.lt c 2048 then .cons (Nat.add 192 (Nat.div c 64)) (.cons (Nat.add 128 (Nat.mod c 64)) .nil) else
  if Nat.lt c 65536 then .cons (Nat.add 224 (Nat.div c 4096))
      (.cons (Nat.add 128 (Nat.mod (Nat.div c 64) 64)) (.cons (Nat.add 128 (Nat.mod c 64)) .nil)) else
  .cons (Nat.add 240 (Nat.div c 262144)) (.cons (Nat.add 128 (Nat.mod (Nat.div c 4096) 64))
    (.cons (Nat.add 128 (Nat.mod (Nat.div c 64) 64)) (.cons (Nat.add 128 (Nat.mod c 64)) .nil)))

-- the UTF-8 byte count of a string (what `Content-Length` counts)
def lspUtf8Len : List Char → Nat
  | .nil => 0
  | .cons c cs =>
    let n := Char.code c;
    Nat.add (if Nat.lt n 128 then 1 else if Nat.lt n 2048 then 2 else if Nat.lt n 65536 then 3 else 4)
      (lspUtf8Len cs)

structure LspHead where
  len : Nat
  got : Bool

def lspSomeHead (h : LspHead) : Option LspHead := .some h
def lspNoneHead : Option LspHead := .none

-- a `Content-Length` line's number
def lspHeaderLen (line : String) : Option Nat := match stripPrefix "Content-Length:" line with
  | .some rest => match readNat (ltrim (charsOf rest)) 0 with
    | .mk n _ => .some n
  | .none => .none

mutual
partial def lspHeaders (h : LspHead) : IO (Option LspHead) :=
  IO.bind (lspReadLine .nil) (fun l => match l with
    | .none => IO.pure lspNoneHead
    | .some line => lspHeaderStep h line)

partial def lspHeaderStep (h : LspHead) (line : String) : IO (Option LspHead) :=
  if strEq line "" then IO.pure (lspSomeHead h)
  else match lspHeaderLen line with
    | .some n => lspHeaders (LspHead.mk n .true)
    | .none => lspHeaders h
end

def lspBody (hd : LspHead) : IO (Option String) := match hd.got with
  | .false => IO.pure lspNoneStr
  | .true => IO.bind (lspReadBytes hd.len .nil) (fun b =>
      IO.pure (lspSomeStr (lspFromBytes (List.reverseOf b .nil))))

def lspMessage : IO (Option String) :=
  IO.bind (lspHeaders (LspHead.mk 0 .false)) (fun h => match h with
    | .none => IO.pure lspNoneStr
    | .some hd => lspBody hd)

-- ## Documents: URIs, paths, directories

partial def lspPercent : List Char → List Nat → List Nat
  | .nil, acc => acc
  | .cons c cs, acc =>
    if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 37 then (match cs with
      | .cons a (.cons b r) => if Bool.and (jHexChar a) (jHexChar b) then
          lspPercent r (List.append acc (.cons (Nat.add (Nat.mul 16 (jHexNum a)) (jHexNum b)) .nil))
        else lspPercent cs (List.append acc (.cons 37 .nil))
      | _ => lspPercent cs (List.append acc (.cons 37 .nil)))
    else lspPercent cs (List.append acc (lspUtf8Bytes (Char.code c)))

-- `file:///a%20b/c.wiz` → `/a b/c.wiz` (as `Wiz.LSP.percentDecode`)
def lspUriPath (uri : String) : String :=
  match stripPrefix "file://" uri with
  | .some rest => lspFromBytes (lspPercent (charsOf rest) .nil)
  | .none => uri

-- everything through the last `/` (`""` when there is none: the working directory)
def lspDirGo : List Char → List Char → List Char → List Char
  | .nil, _, best => best
  | .cons c cs, rev, best => if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 47
      then lspDirGo cs (.cons c rev) (.cons c rev)
      else lspDirGo cs (.cons c rev) best

def lspDir (p : String) : String := match p with
  | .mk cs => String.mk (List.reverseOf (lspDirGo cs .nil .nil) .nil)

structure LspDoc where
  uri : String
  path : String
  text : String
  version : Nat
  /-- (D8 goals) what the last check recorded: body expected types and tactic states -/
  entries : List LspEntry

structure LspState where
  docs : List LspDoc
  roots : List String
  elaborated : Bool
  session : Nat
  closed : Bool

def lspFind : List LspDoc → String → Option LspDoc
  | .nil, _ => .none
  | .cons d rest, uri => if strEq d.uri uri then .some d else lspFind rest uri

def lspPut : List LspDoc → LspDoc → List LspDoc
  | .nil, d => .cons d .nil
  | .cons x rest, d => if strEq x.uri d.uri then .cons d rest else .cons x (lspPut rest d)

def lspErase : List LspDoc → String → List LspDoc
  | .nil, _ => .nil
  | .cons x rest, uri => if strEq x.uri uri then rest else .cons x (lspErase rest uri)

-- ## Diagnostics (the host's `publishDiagnostics` shape)

def lspSev : Sev → Nat
  | .error => 1
  | .warning => 2
  | .info => 3
  | .infoEval => 3

partial def lspDropLines : List Char → Nat → List Char
  | cs, .zero => cs
  | .nil, _ => .nil
  | .cons c cs, k => if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 10 then lspDropLines cs (Nat.sub k 1) else lspDropLines cs k

def lspLineLen : List Char → Nat
  | .nil => 0
  | .cons c cs => if Nat.beq (Char.code c) 10 then 0 else Nat.succ (lspLineLen cs)

-- the line's length in characters (the end of a diagnostic's range)
def lspLineEnd (text : String) (ln : Nat) : Nat := match text with
  | .mk cs => lspLineLen (lspDropLines cs (Nat.sub ln 1))

def lspRange (text : String) (ln col : Nat) : J :=
  let l0 := Nat.sub ln 1;
  let c0 := Nat.sub col 1;
  let e := Nat.max (lspLineEnd text ln) c0;
  .jobj (.ocons "start" (.jobj (.ocons "line" (.jnum (Nat.toString l0))
      (.ocons "character" (.jnum (Nat.toString c0)) .onil)))
    (.ocons "end" (.jobj (.ocons "line" (.jnum (Nat.toString l0))
      (.ocons "character" (.jnum (Nat.toString e)) .onil))) .onil))

-- (D8 goals) a range from character offsets, as the host's `range` (`Wiz/LSP.lean`):
-- start at `start`, end at `stop` (at least one character on, as an empty range is not
-- clickable)
def lspPosJ (p : Pos) : J := match p with
  | .mk line col => .jobj (.ocons "line" (.jnum (Nat.toString (Nat.sub line 1)))
    (.ocons "character" (.jnum (Nat.toString (Nat.sub col 1))) .onil))
def lspRangeOff (text : String) (start stop : Nat) : J :=
  .jobj (.ocons "start" (lspPosJ (lineCol text start))
    (.ocons "end" (lspPosJ (lineCol text (Nat.max stop (Nat.add start 1)))) .onil))

-- (D8 goals) the innermost term entry at `off` (a caret at an entry's end counts, as
-- `Query.termGoalAt`'s `endIn`; ties go to the later entry, and the list is newest
-- first)
structure LspTerm where
  start : Nat
  stop : Nat
  goal : String

def lspTermAt (es : List LspEntry) (off : Nat) : Option LspTerm :=
  match es with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons e rest => match e with
    | .term s t g => match Bool.and (Nat.le s off) (Nat.le off t) with
      | .false => lspTermAt rest off
      | .true => match lspTermAt rest off with
        | .some b => match Nat.le (Nat.sub t s) (Nat.sub b.stop b.start) with
          | .true => .some (LspTerm.mk s t g)
          | .false => .some b
        | .none => .some (LspTerm.mk s t g)
    | .goal _ _ _ => lspTermAt rest off
    | .decl _ _ _ _ _ => lspTermAt rest off

-- (D8 goals) the nearest goal snapshot at or before `off`, inside the `by` block it
-- belongs to (its stop); a later snapshot wins
structure LspGoal where
  start : Nat
  stop : Nat
  goals : List String

def lspGoalAt (es : List LspEntry) (off : Nat) : Option LspGoal :=
  match es with
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons e rest => match e with
    | .goal s t gs => match Bool.and (Nat.le s off) (Nat.le off t) with
      | .false => lspGoalAt rest off
      | .true => match lspGoalAt rest off with
        | .some b => match Nat.le b.start s with
          | .true => .some (LspGoal.mk s t gs)
          | .false => .some b
        | .none => .some (LspGoal.mk s t gs)
    | .term _ _ _ => lspGoalAt rest off
    | .decl _ _ _ _ _ => lspGoalAt rest off

-- (D8 goals) an LSP position as a character offset (`ofPos` in `Wiz/LSP.lean`)
partial def lspOffGo : List Char → Nat → Nat → Nat
  | .nil, _, i => i
  | .cons _ _, .zero, i => i
  | .cons c cs, .succ k, i => match strEqC c 10 with
    | .true => lspOffGo cs k (i + 1)
    | .false => lspOffGo cs (.succ k) (i + 1)
def lspOffOf (text : String) (line col : Nat) : Nat :=
  match text with
  | .mk cs => Nat.add (lspOffGo cs line 0) col

def lspStrList : List String → JList
  | .nil => .jnil
  | .cons s rest => .jcons (.jstr s) (lspStrList rest)

def lspJoin2 : List String → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .cons s .nil => s
  | .cons s rest => String.append (String.append s "\n\n") (lspJoin2 rest)

-- the host's `plainGoals`: the goals in a `wiz` fence (`no goals` when none), the goal
-- strings, and the (empty) trace messages
def lspGoalJson (gs : List String) : J :=
  let rendered := match gs with
    | .nil => "no goals"
    | _ => String.append "```wiz\n" (String.append (lspJoin2 gs) "\n```");
  .jobj (.ocons "rendered" (.jstr rendered)
    (.ocons "goals" (.jarr (lspStrList gs))
    (.ocons "messages" (.jarr .jnil) .onil)))

-- the host's `plainTermGoal`: the expected type and the range of the term it belongs to
def lspTermJson (text : String) (g : LspTerm) : J :=
  .jobj (.ocons "goal" (.jstr g.goal)
    (.ocons "range" (lspRangeOff text g.start g.stop) .onil))

def lspCodeField (code : String) : JObj := match strEq code "" with
  | .true => .onil
  | .false => .ocons "code" (.jstr code) .onil

def lspDiag (text : String) (d : Diag) : J := match d with
  | .mk sev _ ln col msg code =>
    .jobj (.ocons "range" (lspRange text ln col)
      (.ocons "severity" (.jnum (Nat.toString (lspSev sev)))
      (.ocons "source" (.jstr "wiz")
      (.ocons "message" (.jstr msg) (lspCodeField code)))))

def lspDiags (text : String) : List Diag → JList
  | .nil => .jnil
  | .cons d rest => .jcons (lspDiag text d) (lspDiags text rest)

-- a declaration's type line is `check --types` output, not a message: the language
-- server publishes errors and warnings, and `#check`/`#eval`/`#reduce` results
-- (`infoEval`), as the Lean server and the playground shim do
def lspKeep (d : Diag) : Bool := match d with
  | .mk sev _ _ _ _ _ => match sev with
    | .info => .false
    | _ => .true

-- the document's own diagnostics (an imported module's are for its own document)
def lspOnlyFile (path : String) : List Diag → List Diag
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons d rest => match d with
    | .mk _ f _ _ _ _ => match Bool.and (strEq f path) (lspKeep d) with
      | .true => .cons d (lspOnlyFile path rest)
      | .false => lspOnlyFile path rest

-- ## Messages

def lspReply (id : J) (result : J) : J :=
  .jobj (.ocons "jsonrpc" (.jstr "2.0") (.ocons "id" id (.ocons "result" result .onil)))

def lspError (id : J) (code : String) (msg : String) : J :=
  .jobj (.ocons "jsonrpc" (.jstr "2.0") (.ocons "id" id
    (.ocons "error" (.jobj (.ocons "code" (.jnum code) (.ocons "message" (.jstr msg) .onil))) .onil)))

def lspNotifyMsg (method : String) (params : J) : J :=
  .jobj (.ocons "jsonrpc" (.jstr "2.0") (.ocons "method" (.jstr method)
    (.ocons "params" params .onil)))

def lspFrame (body : String) : String :=
  String.append "Content-Length: " (String.append (Nat.toString (lspUtf8Len (charsOf body)))
    (String.append "\r\n\r\n" body))

def lspSend (j : J) : IO Unit := IO.print (lspFrame (jRender j))

-- the host's `capabilities`, restricted to what this server answers (an absent provider
-- is not supported; the shim says `hoverProvider: false` the same way)
def lspInfoviewCaps : J := .jobj (.ocons "version" (.jnum "1")
  (.ocons "methods" (.jarr (.jcons (.jstr "wiz/plainGoal")
    (.jcons (.jstr "wiz/plainTermGoal") .jnil)))
  (.ocons "notifications" (.jarr (.jcons (.jstr "wiz/elaborated") .jnil)) .onil)))

def lspCaps : J := .jobj (.ocons "positionEncoding" (.jstr "utf-16")
  (.ocons "textDocumentSync" (.jnum "1")
  (.ocons "hoverProvider" (.jbool .false)
  (.ocons "experimental" (.jobj (.ocons "wizInfoview" lspInfoviewCaps .onil)) .onil))))

def lspServerInfo : J := .jobj (.ocons "name" (.jstr "wiz-selfhost")
  (.ocons "version" (.jstr wizVersion) .onil))

def lspCapabilities : J :=
  .jobj (.ocons "capabilities" lspCaps (.ocons "serverInfo" lspServerInfo .onil))

-- the workspace roots `initialize` names: `workspaceFolders`, else `rootUri`
def lspFolderRoots : JList → List String
  | .jnil => .nil
  | .jcons v rest => List.append (match v with
      | .jobj fs => match jField fs "uri" with
        | .some (.jstr s) => .cons (lspUriPath s) .nil
        | _ => .nil
      | _ => .nil) (lspFolderRoots rest)

def lspWorkspaceRoots (msg : J) : List String :=
  match jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "workspaceFolders" .nil)) with
  | .some (.jarr xs) => lspFolderRoots xs
  | _ => List.nil

def lspInitRoots (msg : J) : List String :=
  let folders := lspWorkspaceRoots msg;
  match folders with
  | .cons _ _ => folders
  | .nil => match jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "rootUri" .nil)) with
    | .some (.jstr s) => if strEq s "" then List.nil else List.cons (lspUriPath s) List.nil
    | _ => List.nil

-- the last element of `contentChanges` (full sync: it is the whole text)
def jLastText : JList → String
  | .jnil => ""
  | .jcons v .jnil => match v with
    | .jobj fs => jStrOf (jField fs "text")
    | _ => ""
  | .jcons _ t => jLastText t

def lspChangesText (o : Option J) : String := match o with
  | .some (.jarr xs) => jLastText xs
  | _ => ""

def lspHasChanges (o : Option J) : Bool := match o with
  | .some (.jarr (.jcons _ _)) => .true
  | _ => .false

-- ## The session

-- elaborate the document and publish its diagnostics (`check`'s, on the buffer)
def lspCheck (st : LspState) (doc : LspDoc) : IO LspState := do
  hs ← moduleHeaderTexts doc.text;
  let roots := List.cons (lspDir doc.path) st.roots;
  tab ← moduleRootSourcesAs cats tokens roots "Main" doc.path doc.text;
  let run := match modCheckRunHLsp cats tokens hs tab (.cons "Main" .nil) with
    | .mk r _ _ _ => r;
  -- (D8 goals) the document's entries: its body expected types and tactic snapshots
  let doc := { doc with entries := Globals.lspEntries (Run.gs run) };
  let ds := lspOnlyFile doc.path (diagsOf tab (linesOf run));
  let session := Nat.succ st.session;
  lspSend (lspNotifyMsg "textDocument/publishDiagnostics"
    (.jobj (.ocons "uri" (.jstr doc.uri)
      (.ocons "diagnostics" (.jarr (lspDiags doc.text ds)) .onil))));
  sent ← match st.elaborated with
    | .true => lspSend (lspNotifyMsg "wiz/elaborated"
        (.jobj (.ocons "uri" (.jstr doc.uri)
          (.ocons "version" (.jnum (Nat.toString doc.version))
          (.ocons "session" (.jnum (Nat.toString session)) .onil)))))
    | .false => IO.pure ();
  IO.pure (LspState.mk (lspPut st.docs doc) st.roots st.elaborated session st.closed)

def lspDidOpen (st : LspState) (msg : J) : IO LspState := do
  let td := jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "textDocument" .nil));
  let uri := jStrOf (jGet td "uri");
  let text := jStrOf (jGet td "text");
  let version := jNatOf (jGet td "version");
  match strEq uri "" with
  | .true => IO.pure st
  | .false => do
    let doc := LspDoc.mk uri (lspUriPath uri) text version (.nil : List LspEntry);
    lspCheck (LspState.mk (lspPut st.docs doc) st.roots st.elaborated st.session st.closed) doc

def lspDidChange (st : LspState) (msg : J) : IO LspState := do
  let td := jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "textDocument" .nil));
  let uri := jStrOf (jGet td "uri");
  let version := jNatOf (jGet td "version");
  let changes := jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "contentChanges" .nil));
  -- (no change: nothing to publish, as the shim's `didChange` returns)
  match Bool.and (Bool.not (strEq uri "")) (lspHasChanges changes) with
  | .false => IO.pure st
  | .true => do
    let doc := LspDoc.mk uri (lspUriPath uri) (lspChangesText changes) version (.nil : List LspEntry);
    lspCheck (LspState.mk (lspPut st.docs doc) st.roots st.elaborated st.session st.closed) doc

def lspRequest (st : LspState) (id : J) (method : String) (msg : J) : IO LspState :=
  match strEq method "initialize" with
  | .true => do
    let want := jIsTrue (jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "capabilities"
      (.cons "experimental" (.cons "wizElaborated" .nil)))));
    let roots := lspInitRoots msg;
    lspSend (lspReply id lspCapabilities);
    IO.pure (LspState.mk st.docs (List.append roots st.roots) want st.session st.closed)
  | .false => match strEq method "shutdown" with
    | .true => do
      lspSend (lspReply id .jnull);
      IO.pure st
    | .false => match strEq method "wiz/plainGoal" with
      | .true => do
        -- (D8 goals) the nearest snapshot at or before the cursor, inside its `by` block
        let uri := jStrOf (jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "textDocument" (.cons "uri" .nil))));
        let line := jNatOf (jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "position" (.cons "line" .nil))));
        let col := jNatOf (jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "position" (.cons "character" .nil))));
        match lspFind st.docs uri with
        | .some doc => match lspGoalAt doc.entries (lspOffOf doc.text line col) with
          | .some g => lspSend (lspReply id (lspGoalJson g.goals))
          | .none => lspSend (lspReply id .jnull)
        | .none => lspSend (lspReply id .jnull);
        IO.pure st
      | .false => match strEq method "wiz/plainTermGoal" with
        | .true => do
          -- (D8 goals) the innermost recorded term's expected type at the cursor
          let uri := jStrOf (jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "textDocument" (.cons "uri" .nil))));
          let line := jNatOf (jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "position" (.cons "line" .nil))));
          let col := jNatOf (jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "position" (.cons "character" .nil))));
          match lspFind st.docs uri with
          | .some doc => match lspTermAt doc.entries (lspOffOf doc.text line col) with
            | .some g => lspSend (lspReply id (lspTermJson doc.text g))
            | .none => lspSend (lspReply id .jnull)
          | .none => lspSend (lspReply id .jnull);
          IO.pure st
        | .false => match strEq method "textDocument/hover" with
          | .true => do
            lspSend (lspReply id .jnull);
            IO.pure st
          | .false => do
            lspSend (lspError id "-32601" (String.append "the self-hosted server has no " method));
            IO.pure st

def lspNotify (st : LspState) (method : String) (msg : J) : IO LspState :=
  match strEq method "textDocument/didOpen" with
  | .true => lspDidOpen st msg
  | .false => match strEq method "textDocument/didChange" with
    | .true => lspDidChange st msg
    | .false => match strEq method "textDocument/didClose" with
      | .true => do
        let uri := jStrOf (jAt msg (.cons "params" (.cons "textDocument" (.cons "uri" .nil))));
        IO.pure (LspState.mk (lspErase st.docs uri) st.roots st.elaborated st.session st.closed)
      | .false => match strEq method "exit" with
        | .true => IO.pure (LspState.mk st.docs st.roots st.elaborated st.session .true)
        | .false => IO.pure st

def lspHandle (st : LspState) (msg : J) : IO LspState :=
  let method := jStrOf (jGet (.some msg) "method");
  match jGet (.some msg) "id" with
  | .some id => lspRequest st id method msg
  | .none => lspNotify st method msg

def lspStart : LspState :=
  LspState.mk (.nil : List LspDoc) (.nil : List String) .false 0 .false

partial def lspLoop (st : LspState) : IO Unit := do
  mopt ← lspMessage;
  match mopt with
  | .none => IO.pure ()
  | .some body => match jValue (charsOf body) with
    | .none => do
      lspSend (lspError .jnull "-32700" "parse error");
      lspLoop st
    | .some (.mk msg _) => do
      st' ← lspHandle st msg;
      match st'.closed with
      | .true => IO.pure ()
      | .false => lspLoop st'

def lspCmd : IO Unit := lspLoop lspStart

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- dispatch

def kindName : Kind → String
  | .check => "check"
  | .build => "build"
  | .run => "run"
  | .eval => "eval"

-- a command and its arguments as the user wrote them, for `unknown command: …`
def argv (words : List String) : String := joinSpaces words

def parseThen (k : Kind) (args : List String) : IO Unit := do
  cache ← defaultCache;
  match parseOpts args { optsDefault with cache := .some cache } with
  | .version => IO.println versionText
  | .help => IO.println usageText
  -- (the host's `takeTarget`/`--cache-verify` mode errors print the message alone, exit 1)
  | .fail msg => do IO.ePrintln msg; Process.exit 1
  -- (the Lean-hosted `wiz` answers a command without its FILE or with extra arguments
  -- with `unknown command: …`; its flags are positional, and it has no `-o` for check)
  | .err msg => match strEq msg "no FILE" with
    | .true => usageError (String.append "unknown command: " (kindName k))
    | .false => usageError msg
  | .ok o file extra => do
    -- (`--cache-prune`: before the command, so this process has not read what it deletes)
    pruneMaybe o;
    match k with
    | .check => match o.out with
      -- (the host finds the first flag-looking argument; `-o` is not a `check` option)
      | .some _ => usageError "unknown flag: -o"
      | .none => match o.backend with
        | .cons b _ => usageError (String.append "unknown flag: " b)
        | .nil => match extra with
          | .nil => checkCmd o file
          | .cons _ _ => usageError (String.append "unknown command: " (argv (.cons "check" (.cons file extra))))
    | .build => match extra with
      | .nil => match o.out with
        | .none => usageError (String.append "unknown command: " (argv (.cons "build" (.cons file extra))))
        | .some _ => buildCmd o file
      | .cons _ _ => usageError (String.append "unknown command: " (argv (.cons "build" (.cons file extra))))
    | .run => runCmd o file extra
    | .eval => runCmd o file extra

-- (the Lean-hosted `wiz` takes its toolchain flags before the command too:
-- `wiz -I src check f.wiz`, `wiz --cache d build f.wiz -o out`; `-o`/`--cache`/`-I`
-- take a value, the rest do not)
def takesValueFlag (a : String) : Bool :=
  Bool.or (strEq a "-I") (Bool.or (strEq a "--include") (Bool.or (strEq a "-o")
    (Bool.or (strEq a "--cache") (Bool.or (strEq a "--cache-ro") (Bool.or (strEq a "--cache-prune")
      (Bool.or (strEq a "--cache-verify") (Bool.or (strEq a "--target")
        (Bool.or (strEq a "--split") (Bool.or (strEq a "--cc") (Bool.or (strEq a "--rt")
          (Bool.or (strEq a "--cflags") (strEq a "--ldflags"))))))))))))

def knownTopFlag (a : String) : Bool :=
  match stripPrefix "--cache-verify=" a with
  | .some _ => .true
  | .none => Bool.or (takesValueFlag a) (Bool.or (strEq a "--no-cache") (Bool.or (strEq a "-v")
    (Bool.or (strEq a "--verbose") (Bool.or (strEq a "--types")
      (Bool.or (strEq a "--llvm") (Bool.or (strEq a "--wasm")
        (Bool.or (strEq a "--trust-native") (strEq a "--trust-smt"))))))))
inductive LeadSplit where
  | mk (lead : List String) (rest : List String)

-- the flags before the command (values kept beside them) and the rest; a
-- `--version`/`--help`/`-h` ends the flags even though it starts with `-`
partial def splitLeadGo (lead : List String) : List String → LeadSplit
  | .nil => LeadSplit.mk (List.reverseOf lead .nil) .nil
  | .cons a rest => match Bool.or (strEq a "--version") (Bool.or (strEq a "--help") (strEq a "-h")) with
    | .true => LeadSplit.mk (List.reverseOf lead .nil) (.cons a rest)
    | .false => match strStarts "-" a with
      | .false => LeadSplit.mk (List.reverseOf lead .nil) (.cons a rest)
      | .true => match takesValueFlag a with
        | .true => match rest with
          | .nil => LeadSplit.mk (List.reverseOf (.cons a lead) .nil) .nil
          | .cons v r2 => splitLeadGo (.cons v (.cons a lead)) r2
        | .false => splitLeadGo (.cons a lead) rest

-- a leading flag that neither the driver nor the backend knows: host `wiz` errors on
-- it; so does the driver (`unknown flag: …`, exit 2). A value-taking flag's word is its
-- value, not a flag (the host's `parseFlags` consumes it the same way).
partial def unknownTopFlag : List String → Option String
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons a rest => match takesValueFlag a with
    | .true => match rest with
      | .nil => .none
      | .cons _ r2 => unknownTopFlag r2
    | .false => match knownTopFlag a with
      | .true => unknownTopFlag rest
      | .false => match isBackendFlag a with
        | .true => unknownTopFlag rest
        | .false => .some a

def hasBackendFlag : List String → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons a rest => match isBackendFlag a with
    | .true => .true
    | .false => hasBackendFlag rest

def dispatch : List String → IO Unit
  | .nil => legacyCmd .nil
  | .cons a rest => match splitLeadGo .nil (.cons a rest) with
    | .mk lead rest2 => match rest2 with
      -- (`selfhost --rc` and `selfhost` are the one-shot mode; other flags alone are the
      -- host's usage, exit 0)
      | .nil => match unknownTopFlag lead with
        | .some f => usageError (String.append "unknown flag: " f)
        -- (flags alone: the host still validates `--cache-verify MODE` before its usage,
        -- and `--target`'s errors come from `takeTarget`; a valid flag set is the usage,
        -- exit 0, as the host's)
        | .none => match parseOpts lead optsDefault with
          | .err msg => match strEq msg "no FILE" with
            | .true => match hasBackendFlag lead with
              | .true => legacyCmd lead
              | .false => IO.println usageText
            | .false => usageError msg
          | .fail msg => do IO.ePrintln msg; Process.exit 1
          | .ok _ _ _ => IO.println usageText
          | .version => IO.println versionText
          | .help => IO.println usageText
      | .cons b rest3 => match strEq b "check" with
        | .true => parseThen .check (List.append lead rest3)
        | .false => match strEq b "build" with
          | .true => parseThen .build (List.append lead rest3)
          | .false => match strEq b "run" with
            | .true => parseThen .run (List.append lead rest3)
            | .false => match strEq b "eval" with
              | .true => parseThen .eval (List.append lead rest3)
              | .false => match strEq b "version" with
                | .true => IO.println versionText
                | .false => match strEq b "help" with
                  | .true => IO.println usageText
                  | .false => match strEq b "--version" with
                    | .true => match rest3 with
                      | .nil => IO.println versionText
                      | .cons _ _ => usageError "unknown flag: --version"
                    | .false => match strEq b "--help" with
                      | .true => match rest3 with
                        | .nil => IO.println usageText
                        | .cons _ _ => usageError "unknown flag: --help"
                      | .false => match strEq b "-h" with
                        | .true => match rest3 with
                          | .nil => IO.println usageText
                          | .cons _ _ => usageError "unknown flag: -h"
                        | .false => match strEq b "lsp" with
                          -- (`lsp` takes no options: the workspace roots are the ones
                          -- `initialize` names; a flag before it is the host's error)
                          | .true => match lead with
                            | .cons f _ => usageError (String.append "unknown flag: " f)
                            | .nil => match rest3 with
                              | .nil => lspCmd
                              | .cons x _ => match strStarts "-" x with
                                | .true => usageError (String.append "unknown flag: " x)
                                | .false => usageError (String.append "unknown command: " (argv (.cons "lsp" rest3)))
                          | .false => match unknownTopFlag lead with
                            | .some f => usageError (String.append "unknown flag: " f)
                            | .none => match strStarts "-" b with
                              | .true => usageError (String.append "unknown flag: " b)
                              | .false => usageError (String.append "unknown command: " (argv (.cons b rest3)))

-- (`main` is `selfhost/Main.wiz`: the entry point is a module of its own, last.)
end
